{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20","id":1302751,"title":"Low Generation Vampires vs Werewolves? [V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-05T00:34:25-07:00","id":1302751,"title":"Low Generation Vampires vs Werewolves? [V20]","content":"Hello. I was wondering at what generation do combat-focused vampires begin to become comparable to werewolves in a one on one fight in V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T00:54:15-07:00","id":1302753,"title":"","content":"I would say 15 if you could considering ranged weapons like sniper rifles. Probably not what you meant so I go with gen 8 or 9. The discipline spread of the Vampire ist the most important thing to consider here. That being said, a 200 year old 11th combat vampire will probably mop the floor with an cliath who just finished her training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T00:54:26-07:00","id":1302754,"title":"","content":"There's no real metric here. Too much comes down to stats beyond Generation.<br /> <br /> A freshly Embraced 4th Gen that only has Auspex and no significant mundane combat skills, tossed fresh into a ring naked and unarmed with a werewolf? Probably ash in the first turn.<br /> <br /> A combat veteran 13th Gen with maxed out Celerity/Fortitude/Potence, time to prepare buffing their physicals, grab a silver weapon, and catching the werewolf flatfooted? Massive advantage to the vampire.<br /> <br /> Though werewolves are hardly carbon copies either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T01:10:01-07:00","id":1302756,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much asking when vampires gain access to powers that can allow them to win a fight with a werewolf that they just met on the street one night, assuming a werewolf that isn't new but also isn't some legendary god among werewolves. An average werewolf, for as much as that exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T01:28:03-07:00","id":1302757,"title":"","content":"Vampires always have access to such power, it's that developing it all over time that matters. While there are certainly Elder level Disciplines that make you even tougher in combat, and the extra blood pool and blood per turn is nice, and the ability to buy higher base traits... you don't need any of that. Potence 5 and a silver weapon is enough to do in most 'entry' level werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T01:31:52-07:00","id":1302758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302757#post1302757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires always have access to such power, it's that developing it all over time that matters. While there are certainly Elder level Disciplines that make you even tougher in combat, and the extra blood pool and blood per turn is nice, and the ability to buy higher base traits... you don't need any of that. Potence 5 and a silver weapon is enough to do in most 'entry' level werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It's just that I always hear it takes multiple higher generation vampires to take on a werewolf, so I was wondering at what point that is no longer the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T01:34:19-07:00","id":1302759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302756#post1302756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty much asking when vampires gain access to powers that can allow them to win a fight with a werewolf that they just met on the street one night, assuming a werewolf that isn't new but also isn't some legendary god among werewolves. An average werewolf, for as much as that exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Level 1-5 Discipline Powers are sufficient, for that.<br /> The Big difference is that Werewolf have a huge advantage as starting characters. They get their combat shapes, can get addition action with rage, have claws that deal agg damage, and they can soak agg damage with exception of silver weapons, and regenerate damage.<br /> <br /> Vampires catch up with them with enough EXP.<br /> <br /> But it is also dependent on the actual characters, a combat focused vampire with silver weapons (and enough armour), might be able to take down a Werewolf who is not so combat focused even without that many EXP.<br /> Especially if the vampire can avoid close combat and force the Werewolf into a fire fight he has an advantage, silver bullets are quite dangerous for a Werewolf, while bullets only do halved damage against vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T03:24:41-07:00","id":1302772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302756#post1302756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty much asking when vampires gain access to powers that can allow them to win a fight with a werewolf that they just met on the street one night, assuming a werewolf that isn't new but also isn't some legendary god among werewolves. An average werewolf, for as much as that exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, there is no average werewolf, same as there is no average vampire - does the average Vampire have Dominate or not? Do they have Celerity or not? Does the average werewolf have a gift that increases their iniative to &quot;I go first&quot;? Do they have a gift that makes them far more resistant to silver?<br /> <br /> Second, and more importantly, do these characters in any way expect to fight their counterpart? Carrying silver is a great equalizer for vampires, but then again, so is summoning a spirit of sunlight for werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T03:30:27-07:00","id":1302773,"title":"","content":"Two important things to keep in mind;<br /> <br /> - Are these V20 Garou, or W20 Garou? Because that makes an enormous difference really.<br /> <br /> - Garou almost always have an escape button available, Stepping Sideways, which can give them the upper hand in fights. If they're winning, you're done for. If things are starting to look risky for them, they can duck out into the Middle Umbra and wait for a good chance to ambush you.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, Garou are designed for turning monsters into slurry and recovering from any damage thrown at them. If a Vampire is going to kill a Garou it's going to involve doing a lot of damage in 1 or 2 turns, and that means Celerity and/or Potence and an ambush. Far from impossible, but it naturally works in reverse; the Garou will slaughter a Vampire with an ambush. And in a &quot;fair fight&quot; it usually won't be that close, thanks to Regeneration, Rage and the Crinos form, not to mention Gifts.<br /> <br /> And this is assuming a 1;1 fight which is... unfortunately very rare. Garou who are part of the Garou Nation (that is, those who aren't Ronin, their equivalent of Caitiff) tend to travel in Packs, and these packs include multiple other Garou. Beyond that, Kinfolk can be quite dangerous. So while you might get your 5 automatic damage (Potence 5) ambush silver sword in the back move to work, attack twice in that one turn (Celerity 1) and kill a Garou practically instantly... unfortunately their death is going to lead to a LOT of pain for you, unless you can escape without being seen at all (from both sides of the Umbra). So you'll either die in the aftermath or be dragged out into the sunlight by kinfolk at some point, or spend the next few weeks glancing over your shoulder until a furry monstrosity jumps down and turns you to slush in an alleyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:20:56-07:00","id":1302776,"title":"","content":"Also remember that one shotting a Garou, even with Silver, has the problem of after hittng Inc allowing them to roll Rage (diff 8) and instantly regenerate succes levels of health, even aggravated, and pushing them to berserk frenzy. So Garou can come back from seemingly certain death situation once per fight.<br /> <br /> Like others have said, while generation can help if forced to face a Garou it matters far less than proper preparation. As a side note proper preparation for a vampire facing against a Garou is to be somewhere else while your underlings, Ghouls, childer, neonates pawns Etc. ambush the Garou with Silver weapons, preferably ranged ones and with numbers on their side when they are alone without their pack in a manner that the werewolves associates cannot trace back to you. If not properly prepared going to war with Garou is likely to considerably shorten your life expectancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:24:16-07:00","id":1302777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302772#post1302772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, there is no average werewolf, same as there is no average vampire - does the average Vampire have Dominate or not? Do they have Celerity or not? Does the average werewolf have a gift that increases their iniative to &quot;I go first&quot;? Do they have a gift that makes them far more resistant to silver?<br /> <br /> Second, and more importantly, do these characters in any way expect to fight their counterpart? Carrying silver is a great equalizer for vampires, but then again, so is summoning a spirit of sunlight for werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the vampire in question is combat focused? Probably does have Celerity. There would be such a thing as an average vampire or werewolf just as there are average people in real life, the problem is we don't have access to population demographics for supernaturals in regards to how many have a given power, meaning the average for a setting would be decided on by the storyteller. As for the second, I was assuming a scenario in which the two just run into each other, with neither having prepared for the other.<br /> <br /> Edit: Assuming W20 versions of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 04-05-2019, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:56:54-07:00","id":1302781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20#post1302751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I was wondering at what generation do combat-focused vampires begin to become comparable to werewolves in a one on one fight in V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking V20 werewolves or actual Garou from a Werewolf game, because it's basically impossible to beat a Garou using their rules....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:57:19-07:00","id":1302782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302777#post1302777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the vampire in question is combat focused? Probably does have Celerity. There would be such a thing as an average vampire or werewolf just as there are average people in real life, the problem is we don't have access to population demographics for supernaturals in regards to how many have a given power, meaning the average for a setting would be decided on by the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that there just is no average when it comes to werewolves. Where vampires have one splat that determines their primary power set, werewolves have three - the form they were born in, their tribe and the moon phase that determines their duty. What's the average between a trickster, a shaman, a judge, a bard and a warrior? How do you average a king by divine right, a tech-savvy modernist and a collector of forbidden lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:06:01-07:00","id":1302783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302782#post1302782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that there just is no average when it comes to werewolves. Where vampires have one splat that determines their primary power set, werewolves have three - the form they were born in, their tribe and the moon phase that determines their duty. What's the average between a trickster, a shaman, a judge, a bard and a warrior? How do you average a king by divine right, a tech-savvy modernist and a collector of forbidden lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess the same ways you average humans, so either by looking at as many of them as you can or by separating them into categories and averaging those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:12:20-07:00","id":1302784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20#post1302751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I was wondering at what generation do combat-focused vampires begin to become comparable to werewolves in a one on one fight in V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said, it will depend on the build and situation:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is it close combat or ranged combat?</li> <li>Are both prepared to fight each other (silver weapons, daytime, fire sources, buff time, etc), or its a spur of the moment situation?</li> <li>Where are they fighting?</li> <li>What are their Disciplines/Gifts, Merits? <i>Dominate can end a fight before it starts, but a Werewolf merit, Untamable, can make them immune.</i></li> <li>What is the rank of the Werewolf? <i>Gift access depends on Rank, only Elder discipline access requires Generation.</i></li> <li>How much experience do they have?<i> Though without Rank increases,</i> <i>XP is of limited use for Werewolves. </i></li> <li>What Totem traits and ban has the Werewolf if any?</li> <li>Does the Werewolf have a Pack? <i>With a Pack, the Totem cost can be spread out, and the Werewolf has allies that are also strong fighters.</i></li> </ol>W20 close quarters vampire-killing starting build, assumes a Pack with <i>Hummingbird</i> as the Totem and <i>Katanka-Sonnak</i> as a Sept Totem (W20 Rage Across the World, p.29), <b>Ugly McAngry</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Breed: Metis<br /> Auspice: Ahroun<br /> Tribe: Children of Gaia<br /> Nature: Competitor<br /> Demeanor: Soldier<br /> Rank: 1<br /> Physical: Strength 4 (6/8/7/5) (Claws), Dexterity 7 (7/8/9/9) (Dodging), Stamina 1 (3/4/4/3)<br /> Social: Charisma 4 (Imposing), Manipulation 1 (0/0/0/0), Appearance 1 (0/0/1/1)<br /> Mental: Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (Claws), Intimidation 1, Primal-Urge 3<br /> Skills: Etiquette 1, Stealth 3, Survival 1<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Enigmas 3, Investigation 1, Law 1, Medicine 1, Occult 1, Rituals 1<br /> Backgrounds: Fetish 4 (Hunter\u2019s Talons, Mirrorshades), Totem 1 (Hummingbird)<br /> Rage: 5<br /> Gnosis: 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Glory: 2<br /> Honor: 1<br /> Wisdom: 0<br /> Metis deformity: Eyes of Darkness, Tough Hide<br /> Gifts: (1) Jam Weapon, Razor Claws, Sense Wyrm; (2) Spirit of the Fray; (5) Kiss of Helios<br /> Rites: None<br /> Merits: Self-Confident, Untamable<br /> Flaws: Double Jeopardy, Foul Temper, Vengeful (Vampires)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All freebies spent on Brawl, Gnosis, Self-Confident, Untamable, and Willpower; this guy can:<ul><li><b>Win Initiative most of the time. </b><i>Max Dexterity + Max Wits + Spirit of the Fray</i></li> <li><b>Attack up to three times per turn. </b><i>Rage 5</i></li> <li><b>Force weapon using enemies to enter hand-to-hand combat.</b> <i>Jam Weapon</i></li> <li><b>Hit enemies consistently.</b> <i>Max Dexterity + High Brawl + Specialty</i></li> <li><b>Do large amounts of damage. </b><i>High Strength + Claws + Razor Claws + Kiss of Helios + Specialty + Attack roll bonus</i></li> <li><b>Double the damage dice pool against Wyrm creatures, like vampires.</b> <i>Hunter\u2019s Talons</i></li> <li><b>Get lots of automatic successes</b><i><b>.</b> Max Willpower + Self-Confident</i></li> <li><b>Immune to the Dominate discipline</b>, Roll Over, Mastery and Obedience Gifts, able to ignore most forms of mind control<i>. Max Willpower + <i>Untamable</i></i></li> <li>Recover Willpower after each fight<i>. </i><i>Competitor</i></li> <li>Get 2 extra Dexterity dots and the gift: Spirit of the Fray. <i>Hummingbird</i></li> <li>Get access to the gift: Kiss of Helios. <i>Katanka-Sonnak</i></li> <li>Step sideways easily to ambush or escape. <i>Gnosis 5 + Mirrorshades + Willpower + Self-Confident</i></li> <li>Avoid ambushes by Wyrm tainted creatures. <i>Primal-Urge</i><i> + Sense Wyrm</i></li> <li>Regenerate in every form. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Assume Crinos form instantly. <i>Metis</i></li> <li>Soak some damage. <i>Min Stamina + Tough Hide</i></li> <li>See perfectly in darkness<i>. Eyes of Darkness</i></li> <li>Cheap access to some of the best gifts: (1) Falling Touch, Jam Weapon, Mother\u2019s Touch, Razor Claws, Resist Pain, Sense Wyrm; (2) Burrow, Form Mastery, Luna\u2019s Armor, Grandmother\u2019s Touch, Spirit of the Fray, True Fear; (3) Calm the Savage Beast, Chameleon, Combat Healing, Dazzle, Mental Speech, Rage of the Underdog, Shell, Silver Claws, The Cleaving Hoof; (4) Full Moon's Light, Gift of the Porcupine, Lash of Rage, Rattler's Bite, Stoking Fury\u2019s Furnace, Strike the Air, Tenacious Fury; (5) Halo of the Sun, Kiss of Helios, Protean Form, Strength of Will, Totem Gift; (6) Unstoppable Warrior. <i>Metis + Ahroun + Children of Gaia</i></li> <li>Buy future traits as cheaply as possible.</li> </ul><br /> <u><i>One-on-one</i></u><u><i>, in close quarters</i></u>, this character will kill most published 8th (and higher) generation vampire NPCs. Optimized starting vampires also die:<ul><li><b>Celerity 5 (multiple attacks)? </b><br /> Ugly McAngry will go first, has nearly as many actions as the vampire, can make weapons useless (<i>Jam Weapon</i> makes silver daggers or silver bullets useless), it is very good at blocking/dodging, only needs to hit once to kill, and has the option to step sideways if losing.</li> <li><b>Potence 5 (grappling / biting)?</b><br /> Ugly McAngry will go first, he is hard to catch, hard to keep in the grapple (<i>Kiss of Helios</i> will hurt vampires every round of contact and cause R\u00f6tschreck), can take up to 3 extra actions, only needs to hit once to kill, and has the option to step sideways if losing.</li> <li><b>Obtenebration 5 (impossible to harm, lots of damage)? </b><br /> Ugly McAngry will go first and only needs to hit once to kill. It is stronger than the individual tentacle, destroys tentacles easily, and has the option to step sideways to ambush or escape.</li> <li><b>Chimerstry 5?</b><br /> Ugly McAngry will go first and only needs to hit once to kill. <i>Horrid Reality </i>is very strong but the strategy should be one-hit-kill and step sideways.</li> <li><b>Necromancy//Thaumaturgy 5?</b><br /> Ugly McAngry will go first and only needs to hit once to kill. Depending on the Path and builds the powers are instantly deadly (<i>Memento de Morte</i> background and <i>Mortuario </i>merit make <i>Vitreous Path</i> or <i>Path of the Four Humours</i> fatal; same for <i>Path of Conjuring</i> and silver dust or acid), but here the answer is hitting first and leaving the place.</li> <li><b>Animalism/Auspex/Dominate/Fortitude/Presence </b><b>5? </b><br /> HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA. No. Between the immunity to Dominate, Willpower 10, at least 23 initiative rating, and 24 damage dice, none of these are a threat in close quarters.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Combat sequence:<ul><li><b>If surprised</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Reflexively transform to Crinos.</li> <li>Reflexively use <i>Spirit of the Fray</i>.</li> <li>IF massively outnumbered: Activate <i>Mirrorshades</i> and step sideways to ambush later (go to step 3 of the preparation time sequence).</li> <li>IF the enemy has weapons: activate <i>Jam Weapon.</i>\u200b</li> <li>IF enemy is a Vampire/Ghoul/Wyrm-creature: Activate <i>Hunter\u2019s Talon.</i></li> <li>Activate <i>Kiss of Helios.</i></li> <li>Attack. <i>Dice pool of 13 for attacks at difficulty 6</i><i>, and at least 12 dice of damage per attack (24 damage dice vs Wyrm creatures).</i></li> <li>Next turn Rage for extra actions and attack some more.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>With preparation time</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>\u200b\u200b</b>Reflexively transform to Crinos.</li> <li>Activate <i>Mirrorshades</i> for a potential escape.</li> <li>Activate <i>Razor Claws.</i></li> <li>IF enemy is a Vampire/Ghoul/Wyrm-creature: Activate <i>Hunter\u2019s Talons.</i></li> <li>Reflexively use <i>Spirit of the Fray</i>.</li> <li>Activate <i>Kiss of Helios</i>\u200b.</li> <li>IF the enemy has weapons: activate <i>Jam Weapon.</i></li> <li>Rage for extra actions.</li> <li>Attack<i>. Dice pool of 13 for attacks at difficulty 5, and at least 14 dice of damage per attack (28 damage dice vs Wyrm creatures).</i></li> </ol></li> </ul><br /> An alternate build, considering the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack\">Pack</a> as a whole, not so focused on vampires, but even then those guys could kill most stated 6th Generations with little preparation due to sheer numbers and power versatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-19-2026, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:21:55-07:00","id":1302789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As others have said, it will depend on the build and situation: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is it a one-vs-one, one-vs-many, or a many-vs-many fight? <i>You mentioned one on one, but as others have said, werewolves are rarely alone.</i></li> <li>Are they prepared to fight each other (silver weapons, daytime, fire sources, sniper ghouls, etc), or its a spur of the moment situation?</li> <li>What are their Disciplines/Gifts/Merits? Dominate can end a fight before it even starts, but there is a Werewolf merit, Untamable, that makes them immune to it.</li> </ol><br /> All the mayor splats excel at some things: Werewolves at Physical conflict (and Umbra interaction), Vampires at Social (human) challenges, and Mages wipe the others at Mental task (and with <b>preparation </b>time, they can do everything, kill everyone).<br /> <br /> Let me post an optimized combat build using the character creation of W20:<br /> <br /> Breed: Metis<br /> Auspice: Ahroun<br /> Tribe: Children of Gaia<br /> Nature: Soldier<br /> Demeanor: Conformist<br /> Rank: 1<br /> Physical: Strength 4 (6/8/7/5), Dexterity 5 (5/6/7/7), Stamina 1 (3/4/4/3)<br /> Social: Charisma 4, Manipulation 1 (0/0/0/0), Appearance 1 (0/0/1/1)<br /> Mental: Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Intimidation 1, Primal-Urge 3<br /> Skills: Melee 3, Stealth 3, Survival 3<br /> Knowledges: Enigmas 2, Rituals 3<br /> Backgrounds: Ancestors 2, Fetish (Fang Dagger) 3<br /> Rage: 7<br /> Gnosis: 10<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Glory: 2<br /> Honor: 1<br /> Wisdom: 0<br /> Metis deformity: Tough Hide<br /> Gifts: (1) Primal Anger, Razor Claws, Resist Pain<br /> Rites: None<br /> Flaws: Harano Prone, Impatient, Pack Mentality<br /> <br /> Notice that</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your post might have gotten cut off at the end. In regards to your questions, a one on one fight without either preparing in advance, and a vampire and werewolf both with combat-oriented traits. What would it take to beat the example character you provided?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:39:58-07:00","id":1302799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302789#post1302789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think your post might have gotten cut off at the end. In regards to your questions, a one on one fight without either preparing in advance, and a vampire and werewolf both with combat-oriented traits. What would it take to beat the example character you provided?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please check the post again, I have edited it with better redaction, more accurate questions, more combat optimized stats, and an explanation of the werewolf character strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-09-2020, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:43:54-07:00","id":1302801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302758#post1302758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. It's just that I always hear it takes multiple higher generation vampires to take on a werewolf, so I was wondering at what point that is no longer the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>People here on the VtM forum like to hype up Werewolves as the be-all end-all of combat prowess. And yes, they are powerhouses in combat form.<br /> <br /> As a lot of people in this thread seem to have concluded, it comes down to information. Who has a chance to prepare for the fight? (blood buffing, shapeshifting) Who has home turf? Who can arm themselves (silver, fire)? All of these factors play into who wins, even if it is a straight up 1v1 fight.<br /> <br /> And in the pre-battle, the Vampire imo has the advantage. They have so many powers that focus on manipulation, scouting and preparing. Not to mention thaumaturgical rituals...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:54:57-07:00","id":1302803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As others have said, it will depend on the build and situation: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is it close combat or ranged combat? <i>You mentioned one on one, but not the distance from each other.</i></li> <li>Are both prepared to fight each other (silver weapons, daytime, fire sources, buff time, etc), or its a spur of the moment situation?</li> <li>Where are they fighting?</li> <li>What are their Disciplines/Gifts/Merits? Dominate can end a fight before it even starts, but a Werewolf merit, Untamable, can make them immune.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1: One on one, in melee range.<br /> <br /> 2: Spur of the moment.<br /> <br /> 3: Say, in an old abandoned building with no mortals around.<br /> <br /> 4: I was thinking in mostly general terms, but perhaps both with combat-oriented traits and powers? I'm thinking more physical powers as opposed to mind control or more esoteric or social powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:10:30-07:00","id":1302805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pang4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302801#post1302801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the pre-battle, the Vampire imo has the advantage. They have so many powers that focus on manipulation, scouting and preparing. Not to mention thaumaturgical rituals...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you underestimate werewolf gifts and rituals. Rite of the Questing Stone alone is ridiculously powerful, a level 1 rite that lets you find anyone whose name you know.<br /> And of course, there's the benefit of cooperation. When a werewolf says they want to go leech-hunting, their sept will at least try to assist them, limited as their help might be. When a vampire says they want to fight lupines, other vampires tend to want to reach minimum safe distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:25:36-07:00","id":1302809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302805#post1302805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you underestimate werewolf gifts and rituals. Rite of the Questing Stone alone is ridiculously powerful, a level 1 rite that lets you find anyone whose name you know.<br /> And of course, there's the benefit of cooperation. When a werewolf says they want to go leech-hunting, their sept will at least try to assist them, limited as their help might be. When a vampire says they want to fight lupines, other vampires tend to want to reach minimum safe distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your mistake there is in telling the other vampires that they'll be fighting werewolves. <br /> <br /> Just give them guns with silver bullets without mentioning they're silver bullets and send them on their way to take down the &quot;thugs&quot; downtown. Send some ghouls too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:29:02-07:00","id":1302810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302803#post1302803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: One on one, in melee range.<br /> <br /> 2: Spur of the moment.<br /> <br /> 3: Say, in an old abandoned building with no mortals around.<br /> <br /> 4: I was thinking in mostly general terms, but perhaps both with combat-oriented traits and powers? I'm thinking more physical powers as opposed to mind control or more esoteric or social powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To beat nearly <i>everyone </i>in melee as a starting character, I give you the <b>Lasombra Hentai Death-Machine</b> (7 points of flaws needed and must use the optional ruling to start with 4 dots in Disciplines but no Background dots; V20 Core p.85):<br /> <br /> <br /> Clan: Lasombra (Angellis Ater)<br /> Nature: Sociopath<br /> Demeanor: Conniver<br /> Generation: 8th<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 4 (Dodging), Stamina 1<br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 5 (Guile), Appearance 1<br /> Mental: Perception 4 (Sharp Senses), Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Stealth 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Computer 1, Finance 1, Investigation 1, Law 1, Occult 5 (Obtenebration), Politics 1<br /> Disciplines: Obtenebration 5<br /> Backgrounds: Generation 5<br /> Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Merits: Concentration<br /> Flaws: Cold Breeze, Eerie Presence, Lord of the Night, Nightmares<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 15/3<br /> <br /> <br /> The build can attack multiple opponents from the get-go and becomes better with Celerity, Potence, and Fortitude (in that order). A glass cannon, really vulnerable to sunlight, fire and at risk of going late in the initiative order, but if not killed by the initial attack, it can assume <b>Tenebrous Form</b> and become untouchable, key elements of the build:<ul><li>Manipulation 5.</li> <li>Perception 4, Alertness and Awareness 3 (<i>to detect ambushes and react fast</i>).</li> <li>Dexterity 4 and Wits 5 (<i>for initiative</i><i>; Dodge specialty for Dexterity</i>).</li> <li>Occult 5 (<i>Obtenebration specialty</i>).</li> <li>Athletics 3. (<i>with Dexterity 4 and this, a high chance of avoiding attacks while tangible</i>).</li> <li>Obtenebration 5.</li> <li>Background: Generation 5 (<i>Tenebrous Form in one turn, multiple Arms of the Abyss per turn, immune to Dominate from higher generations</i>).</li> <li>Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5</li> <li>Willpower: 10 (<i>this and Generation 5, lets us ignore most forms of mind control, plus granting a lot of automatic successes</i>).</li> <li>Merit: Concentration. (<i>To ignore circumstantial penalties to dice pools or difficulty ratings, helpful to summon tentacles in a stressful situation</i>).</li> <li>Flaw: Cold Breeze, Eerie Presence, Lord of the Night, Nightmares (<i>to have enough points for the build, and when using Abyss Mysticism makes the side effects redundant</i>).</li> </ul>The sequence:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Tenebrous Form</b>. Invulnerable to physical attacks. Envelope opponents to lower their Stamina pool and inflict blind-fight penalties<i>.</i></li> <li><b>Shroud of Night</b>. Lowers opponent's Stamina pool and inflict blind-fight penalties, acts as a source for Arms of the Abyss.</li> <li><b>Arms of the Abyss</b>. Strength and Dexterity 5 each. Use as many Arms as the opponent has actions to hold them, the rest to constrict. Repeat as needed.</li> </ol>For 9 XP you can buy the 3 level ritual of Abyss Mysticism <b>Claiming the Dark</b>, that will make all your physical attributes a 5, gives a -2 difficulty to the first 3 Obtenebration powers, and halves the blood point cost for <b>Arms of the Abyss</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-18-2026, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:47:54-07:00","id":1302814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302803#post1302803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking in mostly general terms, but perhaps both with combat-oriented traits and powers? I'm thinking more physical powers as opposed to mind control or more esoteric or social powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you try to beat Garou in a claw vs fang fight it's going to be difficult...but as most have said, it's not so much a matter of Generation but EXP. Garou have their &quot;reputation&quot; because they start with many bonuses for free including their phenomenal battle form.<br /> <br /> You can get some of these bonuses with Disciplines: Potence 4 it's already better than what Garou have because for a blood point you transform those dice in automatic successes. Celerity can compensate Rage. Fortitude 5 + a good body armor puts you at base Garou level soak. Vampiric fangs aren't as good against them as their claws are against you, but at least cancel their regeneration (not their self resurrection). The problem it's that you need to buy all that.<br /> <br /> I supose a combat focused vampire that's arround Ancilla/Elder levels (200 years of experience) can take an &quot;average Garou&quot; or two in melee, regardless of Generation. Having lower Generation helps, you would need less XP for the build, maybe lowering it to the point you can face a Garou under your conditions with a decent chance of winning being a Neonate with a particularly nasty build (like the one mentioned by <i>Ibeaumanior</i>)...but it isn't mandatory (nor enough by itself) to defeat a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-05-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:58:16-07:00","id":1302815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302809#post1302809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your mistake there is in telling the other vampires that they'll be fighting werewolves.<br /> <br /> Just give them guns with silver bullets without mentioning they're silver bullets and send them on their way to take down the &quot;thugs&quot; downtown. Send some ghouls too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my point, you are not, and most likely will never be, as combat optimized as a Werewolf can be. Vampire strengths lie on social power. Bring some friends, go after its kinfolk, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302814#post1302814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>it's not so much a matter of Generation but EXP</b>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. More experience broadens the options a character has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-03-2019, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T07:30:20-07:00","id":1302818,"title":"","content":"<b><i>For reference, I really know my stuff with Vampire combat.</i></b><br /> <br /> <u>Short Answer:</u> 8th Generation with 100 years experience as Vampire (equivalent of an Ancilla).<br /> <br /> <u>Long Answer:</u> 8th Generation allows 3 blood to be spent per turn (for healing and pumping blood) and that helps a lot. And if the Vampire (or the player) knows how to fight well with the game mechanics, taking out a Werewolf should be doable without silver. With silver, it's easier but we aren't considering disciplines yet. The Werewolf doesn't have to clinch/hold in order to bite for aggravated because he has a snout like a dog. And he already has Crinos claws. Knowing this, we should give the Werewolf respect and recognize he is a combat machine from the get-go.<br /> <br /> The most important things against a Werewolf are either silver or real combat experience. Powers are useful but if you can't dodge or you aren't wearing armor, you're probably dead.<br /> <br /> If you have 3 in any of the physical disciplines, that's a start. Celerity is the best against this foe, but if you're holding silver, a lot of Potence could do him in if you're willing to take a hit or two of aggravated and risk death. Fortitude will only be useful if you have high levels of it against a Werewolf since 99% of his attacks will be aggravated.<br /> <br /> <i>Not including level 5 powers below</i><br /> <br /> Obfuscate is going to be a boon if you can sneak up on him. Level 4 might allow you to disappear or be harder to hit.<br /> Serpentis will give you aggravated soak and a powerful mesmerize ability so you can knife him with your silver dagger without him resisting.<br /> Obtenebration will give you more attacks and more strength, and possibly reduce his stamina which will be INVALUABLE, as well as blinding him.<br /> Protean will give you aggravated damage.<br /> Presence 2 can reduce their dice pools.<br /> Dominate 1 &amp; 2 could stop him in his tracks IF you make eye contact in combat.<br /> Auspex can enhance your Perception checks to notice things but not a lot else unless you want to read his mind (which is usually not helpful in combat)<br /> Dementation can essentially make his decisions a little stupider in combat because he'll be freaking out from phantom sensory input.<br /> Chimerstry could be incredibly useful for imaginative players. Illusions work wonders.<br /> Vicissitude will only be helpful if you have already prepared.<br /> Thaumaturgy is a great weapon if you use it right (each Path differs greatly in usefulness)<br /> Quietus is deadly. Just straight up deadly. I would happily take this over many of the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Almost any level 5 power will give you a <i>great</i> advantage. But... if he has some great Werewolf Gifts, it's back to square one and you're on even footing again as an experienced 8th Generation.<br /> <br /> If you have an older Vampire with worse generation, then the advantages grow with Disciplines and Abilities but they drop off with pumping blood and healing. So you will want better physical stats to start off with since you can't pump blood as fast or heal as fast. If you are a terrible generation as a Vampire but you have combat experience, it really pays off to roll 8-10 dice when attacking because you're easily able to target the eyes and cause blindness. That will make them retreat but they just heal and come back. You need to chop off a leg. You need to blind him. If you have good stats, chop off his god damn leg. Don't just hit him, you're good enough to aim for a particular body part. So take it out. Keep him from running away. Blind him. Blast his teeth out with your shotgun. Remove his ability to act.<br /> <br /> If you are of a strong generation with less experience, you need to really tussle it out physically as your blood pumping is your greatest weapon. You have gotta grapple with him so he can't bite you. Then you gotta bite him.<br /> <br /> All of this changes if you have silver because that becomes your main line of attack. Tremere can levitate silver powder from a pouch and toss it into the Werewolfs fur, clothes, etc. That kind of messes them up. It can shackle their abilities.<br /> <br /> Vampires live longest when they know how to avoid combat so your best bet is to not fight if you have the option because Werewolves are capable opponents from the start. You never fight a capable opponent. You always have someone else do it. Next suggestion is to bring lots of help WITH SILVER if you do fight them. And third, if you're alone, either be extremely adept with brawling (he's gonna get close no matter what), or have a Discipline/Weapon that can stop him in his tracks or hinder his ability to hit you.<br /> <br /> Go for the legs. Go for the eyes. Be good at grappling. Use silver. BE GOOD AT DODGING.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","user":"Knowledgeseeker","date":". 04-05-2019, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:49:24-07:00","id":1302840,"title":"","content":"One advantage Vampires also have if you use the Crossover rules from older editions, is that according to these rules you usually need a power of the same level or higher to counter another power.<br /> <br /> Which means to see for example a Vampire with Obfuscate 5, a Werewolf would need a Level 5 Gift, and most Werewolfs don't have the rank necessary to get level 5 Gifts, while every Vampire can learn level 5 Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we really just look at the Generation as factor, and mostly ignore disciplines and gifts, the vampire needs probably to be at least 6 Gen or lower, at this point he can pump his attributes to levels similar of what a Werewolf gets from his shapes, which should give him and advantage if he also raises his skills above 5. But even then he probably still need a little bit Celerity, armor and silver weapon, to level the playing field. It depends of course also on the edition, since the rules for multi attacks always change. But it would probably still a tough fight.<br /> If you take disciplines into consideration, a Vampire has potentially access to some discipline powers, that could him let take out a most Werewolf quite easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T09:20:58-07:00","id":1302845,"title":"","content":"A starting 13th gen Brujah can solo a 1vs1 fight if built right. Max out potence. Start a grab. Crush their ribs to death. It\u2019s the most powerful combat mechanic. Imbalanced? Sure. But then again plot trumps rules. <br /> <br /> Don\u2019t think I\u2019m cheesy, but I thought of how the twilight movies handled fights. It\u2019d kind be like that. <br /> <br /> As stated earlier, when you fight garou you fight a pack. Not just 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T09:44:28-07:00","id":1302847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302845#post1302845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting 13th gen Brujah can solo a 1vs1 fight if built right. Max out potence. Start a grab. Crush their ribs to death. It\u2019s the most powerful combat mechanic. Imbalanced? Sure. But then again plot trumps rules.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t think I\u2019m cheesy, but I thought of how the twilight movies handled fights. It\u2019d kind be like that.<br /> <br /> As stated earlier, when you fight garou you fight a pack. Not just 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those of us who have never seen the movies, what exactly happened in those Twilight fights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:46:33-07:00","id":1302864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302845#post1302845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting 13th gen Brujah can solo a 1vs1 fight if built right. Max out potence. Start a grab. Crush their ribs to death. It\u2019s the most powerful combat mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a good strategy. Remember to max initiative also, though, as you don't have multiple actions to Dodge at the same time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:36:23-07:00","id":1302880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302847#post1302847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For those of us who have never seen the movies, what exactly happened in those Twilight fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fight scenes had werewolves and vampires zipping around. If the wolves bit them they\u2019d rend body parts off like rice paper. The vampires win tactic was a massive bear hug that cracked spines and crushed ribs. <br /> <br /> Although if a vampire tried that on a pair or more it wouldn\u2019t work cause the second wolf would pop their head off. So you had to be very defensive. That\u2019s why there were a lot of chase scenes. <br /> <br /> Vampires would definitely use an epic clinch. If you use those right tactics In your game you can YouTube those fight scenes to get a feel for how potence level clinching is done right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T12:18:41-07:00","id":1302894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302840#post1302840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One advantage Vampires also have if you use the Crossover rules from older editions, is that according to these rules you usually need a power of the same level or higher to counter another power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd highly advise not using this optional rule in general, but in this theory discussion in specific.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with it here is that Gifts aren't written with it in mind at all. A mage needs Mind 5 to counter Dominate 5 works OK-ish even if the mental shields power in Mind is far less than 5.. you still have it. Since each Gift is independent, there's no guarantee of a higher Rank version of a Gift even existing, and they don't exist in 1-5 rated traits to hand-wave like you can with mages.<br /> <br /> Conversely, there's also plenty of Gifts of any Rank that vampires don't have any obvious &quot;counter&quot; Disciplines for; esp. with Umbra/spirit based stuff. A vampire tries to take out a Ragabash, and the Ragabash just throws on Infectious Laughter (a Rank 1 starter Gift). There's no Discipline that counters this, vampires and ghouls don't have Rage, and if the Ragabash is alone and has Rage 1... they automatically can end a fight against a dozen enemies by having them all too amused by a joke to fight, and just walk away laughing.<br /> <br /> WtA just isn't built for that old crossover idea to work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T12:23:19-07:00","id":1302895,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-05-2019, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:08:25-07:00","id":1302948,"title":"","content":"I have.... no idea what that has to do with what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:33:01-07:00","id":1302953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302840#post1302840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One advantage Vampires also have if you use the Crossover rules from older editions, is that according to these rules you usually need a power of the same level or higher to counter another power.<br /> <br /> Which means to see for example a Vampire with Obfuscate 5, a Werewolf would need a Level 5 Gift, and most Werewolfs don't have the rank necessary to get level 5 Gifts, while every Vampire can learn level 5 Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we really just look at the Generation as factor, and mostly ignore disciplines and gifts, the vampire needs probably to be at least 6 Gen or lower, at this point he can pump his attributes to levels similar of what a Werewolf gets from his shapes, which should give him and advantage if he also raises his skills above 5. But even then he probably still need a little bit Celerity, armor and silver weapon, to level the playing field. It depends of course also on the edition, since the rules for multi attacks always change. But it would probably still a tough fight.<br /> If you take disciplines into consideration, a Vampire has potentially access to some discipline powers, that could him let take out a most Werewolf quite easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be the best way i've ever seen of disspencing with the crazy gift nonsense when it comes to Lupines vs Vampires, thanks for bringing it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T16:58:55-07:00","id":1302961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302948#post1302948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have.... no idea what that has to do with what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, I just opened the wrong thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:11:34-07:00","id":1302965,"title":"","content":"So I see now! Well, yay the work making a bit more sense! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T22:20:03-07:00","id":1303008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302894#post1302894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, there's also plenty of Gifts of any Rank that vampires don't have any obvious &quot;counter&quot; Disciplines for; esp. with Umbra/spirit based stuff. A vampire tries to take out a Ragabash, and the Ragabash just throws on Infectious Laughter (a Rank 1 starter Gift). There's no Discipline that counters this, vampires and ghouls don't have Rage, and if the Ragabash is alone and has Rage 1... they automatically can end a fight against a dozen enemies by having them all too amused by a joke to fight, and just walk away laughing.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC another rule was that you use willpower as substitute for the stats from other games a character doesn't have.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T22:33:02-07:00","id":1303011,"title":"","content":"Except, of course, that WtA is used to Gifts that deal with targets that don't have Rage, and generally accounts for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T23:13:28-07:00","id":1303018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1303011#post1303011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, of course, that WtA is used to Gifts that deal with targets that don't have Rage, and generally accounts for it</div> </div> </div> </div>So how handles WtA Vampiers within it's own rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the general problem when comparing Vampires and Werewolfs is, that Werewolfs get allready a lot of very powerfull stuff built in, with the gifts beeing only the icing on the cake, while Vampires get most of their power from discipines.<br /> <br /> Btw. I was wondering, while Vampires can with the Bloodmagic do something against spirits, can Werewolfs do anything against Wraiths?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T02:35:17-07:00","id":1303035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1303018#post1303018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw. I was wondering, while Vampires can with the Bloodmagic do something against spirits, can Werewolfs do anything against Wraiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two tribes with factions that specialize in dealing with them and some gifts have comparable effects on both spirits and wraiths. But yes, it is far harder for werewolves to interact with wraiths than with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T00:52:17-07:00","id":1303260,"title":"","content":"A couple of years ago there was a guy on the forum who programmed white-room-scenarios between different characters. Can't find it right now, but I remember that it was very interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1914-davidiot","name":"davidiot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T01:11:27-07:00","id":1303263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup\"> Deadliest supernatural warrior: the setup - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/w70vxzd306xfgov/VWFGRougp400y.png?raw=1 A long, long time ago, a contributor on this forum promised to upgrade his combat algorithm to </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1914-davidiot","name":"davidiot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T12:33:03-07:00","id":1523828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302810#post1302810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To beat nearly <i>everyone </i>in melee as a starting character, I give you the <b>Lasombra Hentai Death-Machine</b> (7 points of flaws needed and must use the optional ruling to start with 4 dots in Disciplines but no Background dots; V20 Core p.85):<br /> <br /> <br /> Clan: Lasombra (Angellis Ater)<br /> Nature: Sociopath<br /> Demeanor: Conniver<br /> Generation: 8th<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 4 (Dodging), Stamina 1<br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 5 (Guile), Appearance 1<br /> Mental: Perception 4 (Sharp Senses), Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Stealth 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Computer 1, Finance 1, Investigation 1, Law 1, Occult 5 (Obtenebration), Politics 1<br /> Disciplines: Obtenebration 5<br /> Backgrounds: Generation 5<br /> Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Merits: Concentration<br /> Flaws: Cold Breeze, Eerie Presence, Lord of the Night, Nightmares.<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 15/3<br /> <br /> <br /> The build can attack multiple opponents from the get-go and becomes better with Celerity, Potence, and Fortitude (in that order). A glass cannon, really vulnerable to sunlight, fire and at risk of going late in the initiative order, but if not killed by the initial attack, it can assume <b>Tenebrous Form</b> and become untouchable,<ul><li>Manipulation 5.</li> <li>Perception 4, Alertness and Awareness 3 (<i>to detect ambushes and react fast</i>).</li> <li>Dexterity 4 and Wits 5 (<i>for initiative</i><i>; Dodge specialty for Dexterity</i>).</li> <li>Occult 5 (<i>Obtenebration specialty</i>).</li> <li>Athletics 3. (<i>with Dexterity 4 and this, a high chance of avoiding attacks while tangible</i>).</li> <li>Obtenebration 5.</li> <li>Background: Generation 5 (<i>Tenebrous Form in one turn, multiple Arms of the Abyss per turn, immune to Dominate from higher generations</i>).</li> <li>Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5</li> <li>Willpower: 10 (<i>this and Generation 5, lets us ignore most forms of mind control, plus granting a lot of automatic successes</i>).</li> <li>Merit: Concentration. (<i>to ignore circumstantial penalties to dice pools or difficulty ratings, helpful to summon tentacles in a stressful situation</i>).</li> <li>Flaw: Cold Breeze, Eerie Presence, Lord of the Night, Nightmares. (<i>to have enough points for the build, and when using Abyss Mysticism makes the side effects redundant</i>).</li> </ul>The sequence:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Tenebrous Form</b>. Invulnerable to physical attacks. Envelope opponents to lower their Stamina pool and inflict blind-fight penalties<i>.</i></li> <li><b>Shroud of Night</b>. Lowers opponent's Stamina pool and inflict blind-fight penalties, acts as a source for Arms of the Abyss.</li> <li><b>Arms of the Abyss</b>. Strength and Dexterity 5 each. Use as many Arms as the opponent has actions to hold them, the rest to constrict. Repeat as needed.</li> </ol>For 9 XP you can buy the 3 level ritual of Abyss Mysticism <b>Claiming the Dark</b>, that puts all your physical attributes at 5, gives a -2 difficulty to the first 3 Obtenebration powers, and halves the blood point for <b>Arms of the Abyss</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was a strong build, but I think I have an even stronger one now, again 7 points of flaws needed, must use the optional ruling to start with 4 dots in Disciplines but no Background dots (V20 Core p.85) and makes use of the rules for Necromancy to use Willpower rolls (V20 Rites of the Blood p.130):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Clan: Harbingers of Skulls<br /> Nature: Sociopath<br /> Demeanor: Idealist<br /> Generation: 13th<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 5 (Dodging), Stamina 2<br /> Social: Charisma 1, Manipulation 4 (Guile), Appearance 0<br /> Mental: Perception 4 (Sharp Senses), Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics 3, Investigation 3, Occult 3<br /> Disciplines: Necromancy 5 (Path of the Four Humors 5)<br /> Necromantic Rituals: Death\u2019s Communion<br /> Backgrounds: Memento de Morte 5, Spirit Slaves 1<br /> Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Derangements: Megalomania<br /> Merits: Mortuario<br /> Flaws: Kiss of Death, Inbred 5 (Derangement)<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 10/1<br /> <br /> <br /> The build can kill everything around them at an unbeatable DC, it is at risk of going late in the initiative order, but if not killed by the initial attack, it autowins, key elements of the build:<ul><li>Clan: Harbingers of Skulls (<i>to be able to start with Path of the Four Humors</i>).</li> <li>Necromancy 5 / Path of the Four Humors 5 (<i>Black Breath is DEADLY: unsoakable area of effect attack</i>).</li> <li>Willpower: 10 (<i>the key stat rolled for Necromancy Paths</i>).</li> <li>Derangements: Megalomania (<i>an extra die on Willpower rolls</i>).</li> <li>Background: Memento de Morte 5 (<i>+5 dice to Necromancy rolls</i>).</li> <li>Background: Spirit Slaves 1 (<i>invisible intangible spy who obeys your every command, can create fires and move objects, guard your house during the day, talk to ghosts and do lots of sensitive tasks for you</i>).\u200b\u200b</li> <li>Necromantic Rituals: Death\u2019s Communion (<i>+2</i><i> dice to Necromancy rolls, maybe as a Harbinger of Skulls this Ritual is not available</i>).\u200b\u200b</li> <li>Perception 4, Alertness and Awareness 3 (<i>to detect ambushes and react fast</i>).</li> <li>Dexterity 5 and Wits 5 (<i>for initiative</i><i>; Dodge specialty for Dexterity; Ambushes specialty for Wits</i>).</li> <li>Athletics 3 (<i>with Dexterity 5 and this, a high chance of avoiding attacks)</i>.</li> <li>Stealth 3 (<i>with Dexterity 5 and this, a high chance of staying hidden)</i>.\u200b</li> <li>Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5</li> <li>Merit: Mortuario (<i>-2 diff to Necromancy rolls!!!</i>).</li> <li>Flaws: Kiss of Death, Inbred 5 (Derangement) (<i>to have enough points for the build and get Megalomania</i>).</li> </ul><br /> This is probably the DEADLIEST starting vampire build. At least 16 dice at DC 6 (18 dice if you have the ritual up beforehand, so between 6 and 7 successes), area of effect of 5 meters in diameter per success, if you do not dodge (Dexterity + Athletics) it requires to roll Willpower (DC 8 for mortals or DC 7 for supers) and get more successes than the attacker, or immediately commit suicide if living/fall into torpor if Kindred, it is nearly impossible to get 7 or 8 successes rolling 10 Willpower dice, so those who do not dodge are dead.<br /> <br /> Using Harbingers of Skulls due to starting Necromancy paths, but I think this could be done with a Giovanni... And that releases 2 freebies more to be put into the Spirit Slaves Background, get some Wraiths that help you if you don't win initiative or in the unlikely scenario of enemies surviving the attack.<br /> <br /> You could also use the Nagaraja, and the Vitreous Path. It becomes a single attack, but using Night Cry on yourself as a buff, and then attacking will do around 11 aggravated damage in a single attack against a target. More survivable than the first option if hit, but also more likely to hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-08-2026, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T18:10:22-07:00","id":1523849,"title":"","content":"What stops the victims from spending willpower on the resistance roll, or even just pushing it back turn by turn with willpower until the Vampire is dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T19:09:05-07:00","id":1523854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523849#post1523849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stops the victims from spending willpower on the resistance roll, or even just pushing it back turn by turn with willpower until the Vampire is dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, my understanding is that 1 willpower point grants you 1 success but you need more than the caster of Black Breath obtained (7 or 8) so not possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-09-2023, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T09:53:17-07:00","id":1523916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20#post1302751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I was wondering at what generation do combat-focused vampires begin to become comparable to werewolves in a one on one fight in V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't confuse raw power with great skill or experience when it comes to such encounters. A 5 or 6th generation neonate with no real skill in fighting or survival skills is going to be a bloody smear on the ground against a pack of lupines or a single one where as someone of a much weaker generation but has considerable skills in such matters stand a much better chance against them.<br /> <br /> Mithras, Talley, Theo Bell, Luciata, and Beckett are good enough to fight and kill lupines, but they don't go off in a reckless fashion are try to tilt the odds in their favor as much as they can when it happens.<br /> <br /> My 10th generation Brujah might be skilled enough to fight one, but would rather not face one at all and my 11th generation Malkavian would seek to avoid it all together and would use his skill in Obfuscate, Celerity and Fortitude to get away.<br /> <br /> His viewpoint would be summed up in this quote.<br /> <br /> &quot;Unless your a Gangrel or Ventrue or have considerable faith in our skills to fight them. You are better off to hit hard and fast and get away as quickly as possible from these beasts if you value your neck.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T12:33:23-07:00","id":1523921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523916#post1523916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't confuse raw power with great skill or experience when it comes to such encounters. A 5 or 6th generation neonate with no real skill in fighting or survival skills is going to be a bloody smear on the ground against a pack of lupines or a single one where as someone of a much weaker generation but has considerable skills in such matters stand a much better chance against them.<br /> <br /> Mithras, Talley, Theo Bell, Luciata, and Beckett are good enough to fight and kill lupines, but they don't go off in a reckless fashion are try to tilt the odds in their favor as much as they can when it happens.<br /> <br /> My 10th generation Brujah might be skilled enough to fight one, but would rather not face one at all and my 11th generation Malkavian would seek to avoid it all together and would use his skill in Obfuscate, Celerity and Fortitude to get away.<br /> <br /> His viewpoint would be summed up in this quote.<br /> <br /> &quot;Unless your a Gangrel or Ventrue or have considerable faith in our skills to fight them. You are better off to hit hard and fast and get away as quickly as possible from these beasts if you value your neck.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the original poster was trying to do 1-on-1 comparisons of characters, which is hard (how do equate Generation from a Vampire with Rank for a Werewolf?) so I offered the best possible alternative: starting characters with all allowed Merits and Flaws.<br /> <br /> In general, excepting very specific builds like the Harbinger of Skulls or the Lasombra I posted, an optimized starting Werewolf is far, FAR better at combat than optimized starting Vampires, and that without counting the implicit support of the pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The more you diverge from the premise (Comparison of starter characters) then the weirder things get... Werewolf gifts require rank, so even with 1000's of XP but no rank increases Werewolves hit a ceiling fast. 100's of XP on a vampire could get combination disciplines and more options with regular Disciplines. On the other side, after character generation there is no way to buy Generation increases you either get the background OR start diablerizing people (With all the issues that entails), Werewolves can buy Gnosis and Rage to the top, it would not be the best usage of XP but it can be done.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:05:43-07:00","id":1523927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523854#post1523854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, my understanding is that 1 willpower point grants you 1 success but you need more than the caster of Black Breath obtained (7 or 8) so not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest flaw in the Black Breath strategy is the targets spending WP in the Dexterity + Athletics roll to move away from it, as that only needs one success as long as the character can do so. While Garou aren't big ranged fighters, they'll have the Dexterity to both have very good odds of making that physical avoidance roll, and be decent at throwing improvised weapons at the vampire who really doesn't have a lot of options to defend against ranged fighters. A dedicated ranged fighter (even a human one) could pretty easily devastate the build between having the Dex to move out of range, and easily having the damage output to deal with a vampire that only has Stamina 2 (and Black Breath is 1 bp and 1 wp per activation, so it can't be spammed a lot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:57:37-07:00","id":1523934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523927#post1523927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the biggest flaw in the Black Breath strategy is the targets spending WP in the Dexterity + Athletics roll to move away from it, as that only needs one success as long as the character can do so. While Garou aren't big ranged fighters, they'll have the Dexterity to both have very good odds of making that physical avoidance roll, and be decent at throwing improvised weapons at the vampire who really doesn't have a lot of options to defend against ranged fighters. A dedicated ranged fighter (even a human one) could pretty easily devastate the build between having the Dex to move out of range, and easily having the damage output to deal with a vampire that only has Stamina 2 (and Black Breath is 1 bp and 1 wp per activation, so it can't be spammed a lot).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, totally valid points. Range tends to be the weak point of nearly all splats except mages (Correspondence is the hardest Sphere to counter or emulate for others).<br /> <br /> I name this one as the deadliest vampire starting build thinking the potential area of effect, otherwise I would have made the clan <i>Nagaraja </i>and taken the <i>Vitreous </i>path. <i>Night Cry</i> with 15-17 dice at DC 4 would be around 9-10 aggravated wounds. Assuming the damage is soakable, it is still very very hard to survive it, and even high Fortitude Vampires, or high Stamina Werewolves would be suffering from wound penalties, if not killed outright.<br /> <br /> If allowed to use <i>Night Cry</i>\u200b on themselves for a further -2 DC reduction, then the damage goes 12-14 aggravated wounds. Even with 6 successes on a soak roll enemies still die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I still post that for purposes of this thread my Werewolf <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">Ugly McAngry </a>is the deadliest fighter between Vampires and Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T11:59:53-07:00","id":1523957,"title":"","content":"There are some simple tricks that get a lot of mileage.<br /> <br /> Potence 5*, decent strength, decent brawl.<br /> Use a blood point for Potence, if there's spares, use them on strength.<br /> Roll decent dice pool with 5 automatic successes added. On a success, the target is unable to take <i>any</i> action but try to break loose. Old rules at it's finest. Against this attempt, there's a decent pool with 5 automatic successes on top. Good luck without [automatic successes].<br /> Then bite. The target can take no actions to defend themselves, so it should hit. Deals 5 automatic aggravated damage + successes from roll. Opponent still locked in hold, if they manage to survive, remain active or whatever else. Rinse and repeat. Add a seasoning of celerity to accelerate the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> Retainers 5 (because one might die!)<br /> <br /> Adds +1 (max 4) per retainer to the opposing's attack and defense rolls. It gets one sided quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> *It works with lower, 3 is pretty fine, but is not as guaranteed. Winning initiative can be critical, but once the hold is achieved, it's irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Neither require a particular clan or selective interpretation of rules. Neither requires much of preparation. Neither is flawless either, and [automatic successes] is a good counter to both, but it will solve most problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T18:54:02-07:00","id":1523981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523957#post1523957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some simple tricks that get a lot of mileage.<br /> <br /> Potence 5*, decent strength, decent brawl.<br /> Use a blood point for Potence, if there's spares, use them on strength.<br /> Roll decent dice pool with 5 automatic successes added. On a success, the target is unable to take <i>any</i> action but try to break loose. Old rules at it's finest. Against this attempt, there's a decent pool with 5 automatic successes on top. Good luck without [automatic successes].<br /> Then bite. The target can take no actions to defend themselves, so it should hit. Deals 5 automatic aggravated damage + successes from roll. Opponent still locked in hold, if they manage to survive, remain active or whatever else. Rinse and repeat. Add a seasoning of celerity to accelerate the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> Retainers 5 (because one might die!)<br /> <br /> Adds +1 (max 4) per retainer to the opposing's attack and defense rolls. It gets one sided quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>*It works with lower, 3 is pretty fine, but is not as guaranteed. Winning initiative can be critical, but once the hold is achieved, it's irrelevant.</b><br /> <br /> Neither require a particular clan or selective interpretation of rules. Neither requires much of preparation. Neither is flawless either, and [automatic successes] is a good counter to both, but it will solve most problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocket tag is the best description of the fight constraints. There is a reason that &quot;Spirit of the Fray&quot;, the gift that gives +10 to the initiative of Werewolves, is so strong.<br /> <br /> If you are looking at combat, it becomes an optimization task of maximizing, in this order: Initiative, Attack rolls, Damage, and Dodge. And that makes Dexterity the god stat, as it affects all of those things (to different degrees) at the same time.<br /> <br /> After some point, you are better not fighting at all, using preventive strikes on enemies, looking into esoteric damage sources, or going for things like Dominate + Awe to neutralize threats.\u200b<br /> <br /> Your build is nice at damage but most things will end it before it can do anything. It has no way to guarantee hitting nor to survive if its hit first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T08:08:45-07:00","id":1524001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523981#post1523981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rocket tag is the best description of the fight constraints. There is a reason that &quot;Spirit of the Fray&quot;, the gift that gives +10 to the initiative of Werewolves, is so strong.<br /> <br /> If you are looking at combat, it becomes an optimization task of maximizing, in this order: Initiative, Attack rolls, Damage, and Dodge. And that makes Dexterity the god stat, as it affects all of those things (to different degrees) at the same time.<br /> <br /> After some point, you are better not fighting at all, using preventive strikes on enemies, looking into esoteric damage sources, or going for things like Dominate + Awe to neutralize threats.\u200b<br /> <br /> Your build is nice at damage but most things will end it before it can do anything. It has no way to guarantee hitting nor to survive if its hit first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dexterity is good, I'm not going to argue with that. But it's will blind-side you. Hold uses strength, not dexterity, entirely bypassing that. Strength gets automatic success from Potence, so you would need about 11? 12? higher dice pool to on average match that. <br /> <br /> The thing is, it does not drain a lot of &quot;character resources&quot; and you can actually still make a character out of it. You could go Dexterity 5, Wits 5 with it, if initiative is your thing. There are no restraints, as once again, the power comes from automatic successes, not a particular combination. More dice helps, but you already have such a huge base leap. You could even go somewhere balanced and have a character that's not a one-trick pony. Now, it can't compete with spirit of the fray and the likes, but then we're not even talking starting characters.<br /> <br /> As for defenses, the chance of one-shotting characters with is abysmal without automatic successes or multipliers. It happens. For defenses, you could shore up with class 5 riot gear (-3 to dexterity based dice pools, oh no!), replicating Fortitude 5 in the process. Can still completely fail a soak roll. It happens. But if you want to go &quot;rocket tag&quot;, you have all those options, and unlike throwing a bucket of dice, with 5 automatic successes, you're nearly always guaranteed to win.<br /> <br /> But if you have 5 retainers, one is likely to win the initiative and that's enough. If they manage to use a Hold (ghouls automatically have Potence, increasing the odds), it's over as no other actions than breaking loose is possible, and then you can do whatever.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is that you never need much more than the basic Hold combat manouver. With Potence you just make it fast and effortless. But I'm not sure white-room scenarios will show you that, try it in actual play instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T10:13:10-07:00","id":1524005,"title":"","content":"Set yourself on fire. Vampires can't grab you if you're on fire. Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion can help out here, even from chargen! Otherwise, you'll have to rely on Master of Fire and a tank of gasoline.<br /> <br /> That aside, grappling with Garou and higher-Strength Fera is rather fraught with risk, as they can have both an absurd pool even by elder standards and a specialty. Gurahl don't even have to wait, they just need to have Strength 5 and Rage 10. Bam! Strength 20 in Crinos. Get Brawl 5, and the Deadly Hugbear rides again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T10:51:34-07:00","id":1524007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524005#post1524005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set yourself on fire. Vampires can't grab you if you're on fire. Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion can help out here, even from chargen! Otherwise, you'll have to rely on Master of Fire and a tank of gasoline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, and it'll help prevent the ninjas from catching you as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T12:32:42-07:00","id":1524009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524001#post1524001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dexterity is good, I'm not going to argue with that. But it's will blind-side you. Hold uses strength, not dexterity, entirely bypassing that. Strength gets automatic success from Potence, so you would need about 11? 12? higher dice pool to on average match that.<br /> <br /> The thing is, it does not drain a lot of &quot;character resources&quot; and you can actually still make a character out of it. You could go Dexterity 5, Wits 5 with it, if initiative is your thing. There are no restraints, as once again, the power comes from automatic successes, not a particular combination. More dice helps, but you already have such a huge base leap. You could even go somewhere balanced and have a character that's not a one-trick pony. Now, it can't compete with spirit of the fray and the likes, but then we're not even talking starting characters.<br /> <br /> As for defenses, the chance of one-shotting characters with is abysmal without automatic successes or multipliers. It happens. For defenses, you could shore up with class 5 riot gear (-3 to dexterity based dice pools, oh no!), replicating Fortitude 5 in the process. Can still completely fail a soak roll. It happens. But if you want to go &quot;rocket tag&quot;, you have all those options, and unlike throwing a bucket of dice, with 5 automatic successes, you're nearly always guaranteed to win.<br /> <br /> But if you have 5 retainers, one is likely to win the initiative and that's enough. If they manage to use a Hold (ghouls automatically have Potence, increasing the odds), it's over as no other actions than breaking loose is possible, and then you can do whatever.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is that you never need much more than the basic Hold combat manouver. With Potence you just make it fast and effortless. But I'm not sure white-room scenarios will show you that, try it in actual play instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are confusing what you can do AFTER getting a hold, and what you can do to GET a hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does not matter if you have Strength 10 and Potence 10 IF the opponent has Dexterity 10 and Celerity 10 for example, it would be untouchable for you (and any number of retainers you can field).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> WOD as a whole suffers of the Alpha Strike problem (or the Rocket Tag as I mentioned) i.e. if someone wins initiative (and its able to hit) more often than not, that someone has already won the combat as the hitting options are stronger than the defensive options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine your proposed character somehow magically gets Strength 10 and Potence 10 and no other changes, it will still die against the builds posted in this thread because those builds move first, are accurate (actually hit the opponents), hit very VERY hard, and your proposed build cannot touch back, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T12:35:11-07:00","id":1524010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524005#post1524005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set yourself on fire. Vampires can't grab you if you're on fire. Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion can help out here, even from chargen! Otherwise, you'll have to rely on Master of Fire and a tank of gasoline.<br /> <br /> That aside, grappling with Garou and higher-Strength Fera is rather fraught with risk, as they can have both an absurd pool even by elder standards and a specialty. Gurahl don't even have to wait, they just need to have Strength 5 and Rage 10. Bam! Strength 20 in Crinos. Get Brawl 5, and the Deadly Hugbear rides again.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very oddly situational counter. And that's fine, can't win them all. For the other example, pouring gasoline is followed by the hold. No matches lit. Unless it's a prepared ambush, but there are simply so many easier ways to cheese that.<br /> I'm sure there are many many more counters, but that leaves one vulnerable to the normal dexterity/extra actions mumbo-jumbo. Once again, it's not Potence that's all powerful, it's the way the combat maneuvers hold and multiple opponents work.<br /> <br /> Not even pushing it to the extremes, but even if the vampire has a meager dicepool of 8 after a round of blood (it's a character not singularly focused on doing one thing, but that could be 12 first round, 14 second round and 15 3rd round, if you want to have the same singular focus), but those eight dice are still comparable with nearly 20 in strength + brawl.<br /> Add the 5 retainers, and anyone opposing will be at +4 difficulty on attacks and defenses. Sure, one hold might be lost, but there will be so many of them, and once the Kindred's hold sticks, the bites will be crippling.<br /> And sure, a Gurahl with an extreme focus on the same thing is absolutely lethal, and can probably match or even regularly beat a non-optimized Potence hugger, but the lack of automatic successes when trying to hug back at a difficulty of 9 is tricky. There's just no action economy when swarmed and all actions must be trying to break loose. All that said, the Gurahl would also be a very strong contestant, as hold/bite would work there as well, just a bit more difficult handling high difficulties than a vampire with Potence. A vampire also may only need to use 5-8 blood points (out of 15), while the Gurahl would need to recover all of theirs. In a white room, that's not a problem, but in a game, that can have consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T12:57:49-07:00","id":1524012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524009#post1524009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are confusing what you can do AFTER getting a hold, and what you can do to GET a hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does not matter if you have Strength 10 and Potence 10 IF the opponent has Dexterity 10 and Celerity 10 for example, it would be untouchable for you (and any number of retainers you can field).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> WOD as a whole suffers of the Alpha Strike problem (or the Rocket Tag as I mentioned) i.e. if someone wins initiative (and its able to hit) more often than not, that someone has already won the combat as the hitting options are stronger than the defensive options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine your proposed character somehow magically gets Strength 10 and Potence 10 and no other changes, it will still die against the builds posted in this thread because those builds move first, are accurate (actually hit the opponents), hit very VERY hard, and your proposed build cannot touch back, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please take a moment to read up on combat maneuvers.<br /> You roll strength + brawl to attack with hold. Just like with the Clinch manouver, dexterity is not involved in the roll. Potence (with a blood point in V20) adds your Potence as automatic successes. This means that strength is hit and hold them steady both, both scaling with Potence. The eventual bite uses dexterity, is inaccurate, but the opponent cannot take any actions, so a single successes is all that is needed, and with the 5 automatic successes on damage, that's mostly a game over. But it can be repeated, over and over otherwise.<br /> <br /> If you have strength 10 and Potence 10, you're rolling 10 dice and adding 10 successes. If an opponent has Dexterity and Celerity 10, they roll 20 dice. If there's 4 more combatants on the Potence side, they do it at difficulty 9. You're looking at maybe 14 successes against 3? on average. To break loose, the difficulties does not get added for multiple opponents (doing the literal interpretations here, even if it would make more sense than in many other circumstances), but beating 10 automatic successes is... hard. It's not even a good example, as it only gets better the more Potence is added.<br /> <br /> If you have 10 automatic successes (your example) and your action means your opponent must take an action which where you have 10 automatic successes (once again, your example) you win. At that level it's even breaks the bounds of possibility pretty much to have it any other way.<br /> <br /> If the Celerity wins initiative (likely) they still need to torpor/final death in that single blow (unlikely, but not improbable). If they don't, they loose. If they use the Celerity for extra actions instead, they are even less likely to win, as that one hit needs to win.<br /> I know perfectly well how it plays out in actual game with more realistic attributes.<br /> <br /> Once again, the &quot;build&quot; can be made in multiple different ways, because it's build around how Hold works, not anything else. You can have high initiative with it if you want to go to extremes. But it doesn't need to go extremes. Now against multiple rounds of preparations it falls short, various invulnerabilities are hard. Unless you account for that with kitting out the retainers with things that actually beat them - at this point they are just undefined extra bodies. There are 6 initative rolls, however min-maxed you want them. If one of them wins, any 'unstoppable build' must choose to abort to dodge, or likely be held as the retainer can simply use a willpower to guarantee a hit. If they abort to dodge, they don't get their 'accurate attack' off. And the Potence wielder will get theirs off. Because it's a strength roll. And that means it automatic successes (on the attack-roll) when Potence is fueled, and then it's over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T13:11:42-07:00","id":1524013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524010#post1524010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A very oddly situational counter. And that's fine, can't win them all. For the other example, pouring gasoline is followed by the hold. No matches lit. Unless it's a prepared ambush, but there are simply so many easier ways to cheese that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits of flame would gladly lend a spark. It might be in the form of a favor, it might be in the form of a talen, it might be the rite of the spirit tattoo from Hengeyokai and the Charm: Ignite, but the would-be Blackbeard doesn't have to be the one to do it. Glass Walkers might also have a timed or triggered ignition starter on them for just such a purpose (if fire can only do bashing to you, you might keep one around, too!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure there are many many more counters, but that leaves one vulnerable to the normal dexterity/extra actions mumbo-jumbo. Once again, it's not Potence that's all powerful, it's the way the combat maneuvers hold and multiple opponents work. </div> </div> </div>And they can all shred themselves into bloody strips if they try wrestling someone with Teeth of the Skin/Gift of the Porcupine!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not even pushing it to the extremes, but even if the vampire has a meager dicepool of 8 after a round of blood (it's a character not singularly focused on doing one thing, but that could be 12 first round, 14 second round and 15 3rd round, if you want to have the same singular focus), but those eight dice are still comparable with nearly 20 in strength + brawl.<br /> Add the 5 retainers, and anyone opposing will be at +4 difficulty on attacks and defenses. Sure, one hold might be lost, but there will be so many of them, and once the Kindred's hold sticks, the bites will be crippling. </div> </div> </div>Or the Gurahl could throw a car or truck at the renfields and then go for the vampire. Possibly roll it along, Katamari Damacy style, until it gets wet and red from ghoul juice. Maybe takes the vampire out, too. If throwing takes too long, though, I suppose the bear could just use it as an area effect weapon, Aberrant-style. Strength 20 is already beyond the list of feats for W20. Technically, it would also allow the Gurahl to relocate way more quickly than the ghouls could keep up with, via jumping. It wouldn't be out of the question to do a Matrix leap by Strength alone... or maybe a belly flop. Strength 20 opens a lot of doors. Bank vaults, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sure, a Gurahl with an extreme focus on the same thing is absolutely lethal, </div> </div> </div>That's not really an extreme focus. Rage is cheap to raise, Strength can start out high enough, and it's only four freebies to get Brawl 5. Which, if they're an Uzmati, is perfectly within their balliwick to practice.<br /> <br /> An extreme focus would be getting a bunch of Gifts out of breed to do the &quot;see how much damage you can do with a fang dagger!&quot; challenge, like using Might of Thor and Coup de Grace. This is just a few freebies at chargen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and can probably match or even regularly beat a non-optimized Potence hugger, but the lack of automatic successes when trying to hug back at a difficulty of 9 is tricky. There's just no action economy when swarmed and all actions must be trying to break loose. All that said, the Gurahl would also be a very strong contestant, as hold/bite would work there as well, just a bit more difficult handling high difficulties than a vampire with Potence. A vampire also may only need to use 5-8 blood points (out of 15), while the Gurahl would need to recover all of theirs. In a white room, that's not a problem, but in a game, that can have consequences. </div> </div> </div>The Gurahl, again, can grapple at range. Or just go from being able to hurling pickups for distance to being able to drop a building on you with Desperate Strength. That, again, at least takes care of the ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T14:59:57-07:00","id":1524015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524013#post1524013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits of flame would gladly lend a spark. It might be in the form of a favor, it might be in the form of a talen, it might be the rite of the spirit tattoo from Hengeyokai and the Charm: Ignite, but the would-be Blackbeard doesn't have to be the one to do it. Glass Walkers might also have a timed or triggered ignition starter on them for just such a purpose (if fire can only do bashing to you, you might keep one around, too!).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And they can all shred themselves into bloody strips if they try wrestling someone with Teeth of the Skin/Gift of the Porcupine!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or the Gurahl could throw a car or truck at the renfields and then go for the vampire. Possibly roll it along, Katamari Damacy style, until it gets wet and red from ghoul juice. Maybe takes the vampire out, too. If throwing takes too long, though, I suppose the bear could just use it as an area effect weapon, Aberrant-style. Strength 20 is already beyond the list of feats for W20. Technically, it would also allow the Gurahl to relocate way more quickly than the ghouls could keep up with, via jumping. It wouldn't be out of the question to do a Matrix leap by Strength alone... or maybe a belly flop. Strength 20 opens a lot of doors. Bank vaults, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not really an extreme focus. Rage is cheap to raise, Strength can start out high enough, and it's only four freebies to get Brawl 5. Which, if they're an Uzmati, is perfectly within their balliwick to practice.<br /> <br /> An extreme focus would be getting a bunch of Gifts out of breed to do the &quot;see how much damage you can do with a fang dagger!&quot; challenge, like using Might of Thor and Coup de Grace. This is just a few freebies at chargen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Gurahl, again, can grapple at range. Or just go from being able to hurling pickups for distance to being able to drop a building on you with Desperate Strength. That, again, at least takes care of the ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>If using an outside force, it gets quite unpredictable fast. At that point, the werewolf pack is the reasonable and credential threat, and that takes out any advantages presented. Perhaps the vampire can off one werewolf, but that's a big if when they are not controlled by spiraling difficulties (and able to use those in return) and uncontrolled multiple actions. If it's an activation required, it's still another action. But once again, it's so oddly specific counters that fill little to no purpose against anything else. But they exist, and that's fine! Perhaps werewolves after reading holding rules institute the gift as mandatory with gasoline baths and self-ignitions talens set. Creates all other sorts of problems, but it's definitely a good counter to this. But the counter to that will be something that abuses hold and multiple opponents and isn't as affected by fire, and it starts all over again.<br /> <br /> A level 4 gift is a nice counter, but it only protects against the bite damage, as the hold does not strike - and even if it did, it has 5 automatic successes, bypassing that critera. Instead of that, it's the feeding bite, which does no damage, and is a bit slower, but just as inevitable. It might rip up a ghoul though. Good thing there's a spare.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected on the build, that sounds reasonable.<br /> I have not played Gurahl, but they do have some issues recovering Rage do they not? While not a problem in a white-room, someone instantly blowing all their rage (they don't have the rage per turn that wolves have either?) at first sign of conflict is exceedingly unlikely to have a full pool in play.<br /> <br /> These are amazing things that displays how high strength can be played, and strategically moving about.<br /> Unfortunately, the rules put some stop to it, as a kindergarterer backed by a willpower will hug that 20 strength bear, and force them as their next action to remove the grip. It's the lockdown of hold that's the killer. You could do all these amazing things, but the hold forces you to only break loose, regardless how silly it might be. It would probably be houseruled within in a second at a table, but that's how it's written. <br /> Doesn't matter how many things you could do if you had freedom of choice, if a ghoul grapples, all you can do is avoid it, which removes any offensive actions, or be grappled and then all you can do is break loose. And if they do win initiative, attacks are made at +4 difficulty, which makes anything really dodgeable. And even if it strikes, it does not automatically make it an area effect that can take out the retainers.<br /> <br /> It's not really any powers that cause it, it's the way the hold and the multiple opponents maneuvers are written that's the core issue. Potence and Retainers simply ensures those are constantly in play. There are likely ways to make it even better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T16:40:32-07:00","id":1524020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524012#post1524012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Celerity wins initiative (likely) they still need to torpor/final death in that single blow (unlikely, but not improbable). If they don't, they loose. If they use the Celerity for extra actions instead, they are even less likely to win, as that one hit needs to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do they need to win in one hit? Dexterity 10 and Celerity 10 means they can be forever out of reach of the Potence grappler. Win Init, move away, either go really far away if you're dealing with a lot of enemies alone, or stay a bit closer and start kiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T20:56:03-07:00","id":1524031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524015#post1524015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If using an outside force, it gets quite unpredictable fast. At that point, the werewolf pack is the reasonable and credential threat, and that takes out any advantages presented. Perhaps the vampire can off one werewolf, but that's a big if when they are not controlled by spiraling difficulties (and able to use those in return) and uncontrolled multiple actions. If it's an activation required, it's still another action. But once again, it's so oddly specific counters that fill little to no purpose against anything else. But they exist, and that's fine! Perhaps werewolves after reading holding rules institute the gift as mandatory with gasoline baths and self-ignitions talens set. Creates all other sorts of problems, but it's definitely a good counter to this. But the counter to that will be something that abuses hold and multiple opponents and isn't as affected by fire, and it starts all over again.<br /> <br /> A level 4 gift is a nice counter, but it only protects against the bite damage, as the hold does not strike - and even if it did, it has 5 automatic successes, bypassing that critera. Instead of that, it's the feeding bite, which does no damage, and is a bit slower, but just as inevitable. It might rip up a ghoul though. Good thing there's a spare.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a starting Gift for Rokea (it's only as high as it is for Garou because it's weird for them and their fur), and it inflicts damage to anyone that the user is grappling, tackling, or immobilizing; as they're still grappling with someone while being grappled, the damage probably still applies to anyone, you know, holding them tightly, which would include all the ghouls and the vampire. Being made of magic teeth makes wrestling really difficult... for other people. Also, going off of Strength alone would probably catch a ruling for not being able to evade the effects of it no matter what, since you're not being careful or skillful enough to avoid the mass of blades when you put your face into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I stand corrected on the build, that sounds reasonable.<br /> I have not played Gurahl, but they do have some issues recovering Rage do they not? While not a problem in a white-room, someone instantly blowing all their rage (they don't have the rage per turn that wolves have either?) at first sign of conflict is exceedingly unlikely to have a full pool in play. </div> </div> </div>There's ways around it. If nothing else, they still get Silver Claws, but I'd expect that being born to be the antithesis of what a vampire represents would probably refill their Rage pretty quickly in a confrontation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are amazing things that displays how high strength can be played, and strategically moving about.<br /> Unfortunately, the rules put some stop to it, as a kindergarterer backed by a willpower will hug that 20 strength bear, and force them as their next action to remove the grip. It's the lockdown of hold that's the killer. You could do all these amazing things, but the hold forces you to only break loose, regardless how silly it might be. It would probably be houseruled within in a second at a table, but that's how it's written. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need to be houseruled as such; Werewolf has plenty of exceptions for things like that, like Crinos punches still inflicting lethal damage, that the force the hypothetical child can muster doesn't mean shit, WP or not. In any case, I think that we can get a guest ruling in from Exalted 3e and say that if you can't operate on the same size scale as your opponent, then you're out of luck. Conveniently, this means that the Gurahl wouldn't be impeded by the ghouls or possibly even the vampire, because being 20 feet tall and likely over four tons is probably a bit much for even Kindred with Potence 5 to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't matter how many things you could do if you had freedom of choice, if a ghoul grapples, all you can do is avoid it, which removes any offensive actions, or be grappled and then all you can do is break loose. And if they do win initiative, attacks are made at +4 difficulty, which makes anything really dodgeable. And even if it strikes, it does not automatically make it an area effect that can take out the retainers.<br /> <br /> It's not really any powers that cause it, it's the way the hold and the multiple opponents maneuvers are written that's the core issue. Potence and Retainers simply ensures those are constantly in play. There are likely ways to make it even better. </div> </div> </div>Crush means making a grappling roll from (Honor) yards away. So, for a rank 3, minimum, that'd easily be around 15 feet, at which point the vampire simply gets mysteriously rikosinot-ed high up into the air and comes down as a rain of limbs (Garou and Fera in war forms do agg in grapples thanks to their massive claws, so with Strength 20 and Brawl 6, that's... a shitload of agg, like easily 20 levels), before the lick or the ghouls can get nearby. In comparison, throwing a truck for an area attack would be a happy fun kid gloves maneuver.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T01:31:29-07:00","id":1524033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524020#post1524020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do they need to win in one hit? Dexterity 10 and Celerity 10 means they can be forever out of reach of the Potence grappler. Win Init, move away, either go really far away if you're dealing with a lot of enemies alone, or stay a bit closer and start kiting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don\u2019t use blood for extra actions, they win imitative. They can run away, sure.<br /> if they use it for their extra actions, they risk loosing initiative, and any attack they make is at difficulty +4, and delayed actions means that even if they they win initiative, run away with their action and then run back in during celerity and strike, their opponents can now take their actions.<br /> Granted, staying at range and plinking away is an effective strategy, in particular if there\u2019s enough celerity actions reserved for dodging the absolutely devastating return throws from the Potence Kindred and the plinking from the ghouls. It\u2019s all about who gets an unlucky break or runs out of juice, but the Celerity user can still leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T01:53:12-07:00","id":1524034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524031#post1524031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a starting Gift for Rokea (it's only as high as it is for Garou because it's weird for them and their fur), and it inflicts damage to anyone that the user is grappling, tackling, or immobilizing; as they're still grappling with someone while being grappled, the damage probably still applies to anyone, you know, holding them tightly, which would include all the ghouls and the vampire. Being made of magic teeth makes wrestling really difficult... for other people. Also, going off of Strength alone would probably catch a ruling for not being able to evade the effects of it no matter what, since you're not being careful or skillful enough to avoid the mass of blades when you put your face into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's ways around it. If nothing else, they still get Silver Claws, but I'd expect that being born to be the antithesis of what a vampire represents would probably refill their Rage pretty quickly in a confrontation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be houseruled as such; Werewolf has plenty of exceptions for things like that, like Crinos punches still inflicting lethal damage, that the force the hypothetical child can muster doesn't mean shit, WP or not. In any case, I think that we can get a guest ruling in from Exalted 3e and say that if you can't operate on the same size scale as your opponent, then you're out of luck. Conveniently, this means that the Gurahl wouldn't be impeded by the ghouls or possibly even the vampire, because being 20 feet tall and likely over four tons is probably a bit much for even Kindred with Potence 5 to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Crush means making a grappling roll from (Honor) yards away. So, for a rank 3, minimum, that'd easily be around 15 feet, at which point the vampire simply gets mysteriously rikosinot-ed high up into the air and comes down as a rain of limbs (Garou and Fera in war forms do agg in grapples thanks to their massive claws, so with Strength 20 and Brawl 6, that's... a shitload of agg, like easily 20 levels), before the lick or the ghouls can get nearby. In comparison, throwing a truck for an area attack would be a happy fun kid gloves maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a good gift at rank 1 for a Rokea, but the emphasis is that they are the active user. Now, it\u2019s scary for the ghouls, but unlikely to kill in a hit, so they can still get the first hold in, preventing offensive actions.<br /> <br /> You are citing interpretations and house rulings and another would be using strength breaks them and that\u2019s why there\u2019s no damage taken at 5+ successes. Strikes is a loose term, but at the best interpreting it means rokea are immune to the biting, but will die slowly to ghouls stabbing instead, as a knife renders them immune to it. <br /> <br /> Silver claws is rank 1? What are the actual rules on refilling rage and spendings per turn by the book? Because if you can\u2019t get the +10 straight away, chances are ever in the Kindreds favor.<br /> <br /> Yea, you can rule however you want, that\u2019s what the golden rule is for, but if you want to have an argument, what we have is what\u2019s written. Nothing wrong with deviating from that at the table, I know we ignored multiple combatants and hold rules pretty fast, but that doesn\u2019t make it less of a house rule. You can talk about scales and what not, but that\u2019s from other games. Does it make sense? Very much. Is that the rules? No.<br /> <br /> If. <br /> If it\u2019s a rank 3, you can add ridiculous amounts of things to the Kindred. If it wins the initiative against 6 characters. A character made from vampire uses the vampire rule book. Their holds allow no damage (that\u2019s clinch). If werewolves have a maneuver that deals aggravated called grapple, that\u2019s what they would use, but if they loose initiative they will not have any actions of their choosing. And if they do win, it\u2019s at difficulty 9, meaning the target can abort to defend and likely win despite having a minuscule dice pool. 26 dice at difficulty 9 is 2-3 successes, while the chance of botching is nearly non-existent. If the werewolf doesn\u2019t have a difficulty cap at 9, then it\u2019s by average 0 successes at difficulty 10, with a possibility of botching (if low) Now, if it hits, it\u2019s bye bye to the target most likely, but there are so many ifs and assumptions and house rulings for that to be likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T07:18:25-07:00","id":1524040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524034#post1524034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a good gift at rank 1 for a Rokea, but the emphasis is that they are the active user.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes no sense. Anyone trying to grab someone made out of magic razor teeth should be cutting themselves as a matter of course. There's nowhere to grip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, it\u2019s scary for the ghouls, but unlikely to kill in a hit, so they can still get the first hold in, preventing offensive actions. </div> </div> </div>If it does more damage than their Stamina, they're stunned and presumably aren't holding on to anyone well enough to count as, well, holding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are citing interpretations and house rulings and another would be using strength breaks them and that\u2019s why there\u2019s no damage taken at 5+ successes. Strikes is a loose term, but at the best interpreting it means rokea are immune to the biting, but will die slowly to ghouls stabbing instead, as a knife renders them immune to it. </div> </div> </div>If the ghouls are stabbing they aren't grabbing. Why are you blabbing? We have more important things for gabbing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver claws is rank 1? What are the actual rules on refilling rage and spendings per turn by the book? Because if you can\u2019t get the +10 straight away, chances are ever in the Kindreds favor. </div> </div> </div>No, of course it isn't a rank one Gift, but the terms of this are rather fluid and open, since, as has been noted up thread, Garou and Fera tend to progress along a development path whereas Kindred largely don't. As for Rage recovery, it can be frustratingly arbitrary, but even if the moon isn't out and the character is oddly focused around the vampires, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DuWEEKeJLMI\" target=\"_blank\">there's one more option</a>. Only, you know, with spiritually awakened drugs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yea, you can rule however you want, that\u2019s what the golden rule is for, but if you want to have an argument, what we have is what\u2019s written. Nothing wrong with deviating from that at the table, I know we ignored multiple combatants and hold rules pretty fast, but that doesn\u2019t make it less of a house rule. You can talk about scales and what not, but that\u2019s from other games. Does it make sense? Very much. Is that the rules? No. </div> </div> </div>It is in the rules of a very similar rules set, and it fills in where the ST system is blinkered stupid because it didn't think about the consequences of letting people be 20 plus foot tall monsters that are made of iron. It excuses a bunch of other shit, so why stop here? Especially when it clearly made bridges and inroads to trying to cover this with V20's original vehicular homicide rules (Hunter's Hunted 2, great for taking out vampires!)?<br /> <br /> Just like ghouls can't hold a fucking truck barreling down the road, they're chaff before a conservatively four tonne monster that has Strength literally off the scale of the feats of strength chart (topping out at 15, well short of the Gurahl's capacity for sustaining 20 for several turns, and expansible beyond even that that for a bit of bashing damage). And the only rules adjustments that we're likely to get... well, VV5 doesn't like people playing with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If.<br /> If it\u2019s a rank 3, you can add ridiculous amounts of things to the Kindred </div> </div> </div>Not really. You could get to Rank 3 in like, two months if you're really active, no joke. Kindred rarely advance so ambitiously, and if they do, they're typically going to get stabbed in the back by other Kindred for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . If it wins the initiative against 6 characters. A character made from vampire uses the vampire rule book. Their holds allow no damage (that\u2019s clinch). If werewolves have a maneuver that deals aggravated called grapple, that\u2019s what they would use, but if they loose initiative they will not have any actions of their choosing. And if they do win, it\u2019s at difficulty 9, meaning the target can abort to defend and likely win despite having a minuscule dice pool. 26 dice at difficulty 9 is 2-3 successes, while the chance of botching is nearly non-existent. If the werewolf doesn\u2019t have a difficulty cap at 9, then it\u2019s by average 0 successes at difficulty 10, with a possibility of botching (if low) Now, if it hits, it\u2019s bye bye to the target most likely, but there are so many ifs and assumptions and house rulings for that to be likely. </div> </div> </div>No, see, it's not melee. It's a ranged attack. Crush means that you make the Grappling attack at range and the target suddenly gets torn to pieces in a horrific spectacle of gore. The ghouls are left agog at their boss being turned into a grisly (and possibly grizzly!) spectacle and probably at least a little in shock due to the blood bond. Don't trifle with werebeasts, or you'll find out what it's like to exist in a setting that has a lot in common with Splatterhouse.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T16:43:51-07:00","id":1524054,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12225\" data-vbnamecard=\"12225\">Trassel</a> To make it simple, post your desired stats, both for the Potence Vampire and its opponents and pick the location/circumstances; we will use the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OK1pf7N3tIoPYYhX0kL37s-awQ0owwKNZlopwZ4EjHI/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">OWOD probability calculator</a>\u200b to see the likelihood of success and see if that suffices.\u200b<br /> <br /> I did half the work for you because I have posted in this thread full stats for a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">Werewolf</a>, a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302810#post1302810\">Lasombra</a>, and a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523828#post1523828\">Harbinger of Skulls</a>, with the strategies each would use, all being built as starting characters.<br /> <br /> My belief is that the Werewolf build would overwhelm most starting characters if full frontal attacks are used, but please post your full build and prove me wrong. Mention any restrictions, conditions, etc, that you want applied; I would however in spirit of fairness ask to consider that if you assume preparation time for the Potence Vampire, the same be assumed for the opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T23:07:40-07:00","id":1524185,"title":"","content":"I think if we restrict this purely to physical combat, and disciplines/gifts that raise your combat ability directly, and ignore all the &quot;autowin&quot; disciplines/gifts (I mean both splats have at higher levels enough powers of the type that if you optimise for them and go first in combat your opponent is done) I think the point where Vampires really get something that could pushes them in physical combat way above Werewolfs would be 6. Gen, and here specifically the Celerity Power &quot;Flower of Death&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think in actual game a Vampire Char surpassing a Werewolf Chat with the same amount of XP will likely ever happen, since Werewolfs just start more powerful and their Gifts are simply cheaper (not mention that you can cherry pick what gifts you want while vampires will often need to acquire some pretty lack lustre powers to get to the good stuff), and often more powerful than equivalent discipline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T16:55:54-07:00","id":1524207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524185#post1524185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if we restrict this purely to physical combat, and disciplines/gifts that raise your combat ability directly, and ignore all the &quot;autowin&quot; disciplines/gifts (I mean both splats have at higher levels enough powers of the type that if you optimise for them and go first in combat your opponent is done) I think the point where Vampires really get something that could pushes them in physical combat way above Werewolfs would be 6. Gen, and here specifically the Celerity Power &quot;Flower of Death&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think in actual game a Vampire Char surpassing a Werewolf Chat with the same amount of XP will likely ever happen, since Werewolfs just start more powerful and their Gifts are simply cheaper (not mention that you can cherry pick what gifts you want while vampires will often need to acquire some pretty lack lustre powers to get to the good stuff), and often more powerful than equivalent discipline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flower of Death is only for hand to hand, though, so you'd have to risk coming within arm's reach of a character with a staggeringly higher Strength (say, by using Gift of the Spriggan or Warp-Fury* for the most mid-tribe of all) and getting grappled. Spirit of the Fray means that they can wait for you to do this and interrupt you. Several tribes can also just flat out wait for you to waste massive amounts of blood trying to hit them while Strike the Air is engaged, and you'd need all the extra dice from Flower of Death just to try hitting a high-Rank Stargazer (literally nothing beats Circular Attack now, it can flat out give you Exalted-style perfect dodges in addition to being able to just redirect an attack to someone else).<br /> <br /> Of course, range is also a possible Achilles' heel for the lick you've proposed. Most of these solutions are Rank 3 or higher, but they're also in the style of &quot;dump damage on target, they have to deal with it&quot;, like Electroshock, which can be targeted from far off and rather unobtrusively just as long as the Glass Walker can connect a circuit. Red Talons, in contrast, can just howl at you if they can see you, and you take levels of lethal. Not agg, but they don't have to spend anything to do it.<br /> <br /> There's also Gift of the Giants, which allows Garou to Ultraman up to any size to become bigger than the biggest thing in the scene. A wonderfully versatile trick from Apocalypse that can be used in response to anything with higher physical stats than you to get higher stats than them. The only downside is that you're unlikely to learn it readily outside end of the world scenarios, where you typically have more important enemies to fight, like Grandmother Thunderwyrm or the zmei.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, there may be something from Vampire that outstrips Garou combat capacities, but it's not Flower of Death.<br /> <br /> *See Werewolf: the Wyld West. The tl;dr is that it's a potential one way ride that injures the Garou significantly at the end but boy does it pack a punch before that, basically doubling Crinos stats, and then some for Dexterity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T12:58:29-07:00","id":1524233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524185#post1524185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if we restrict this purely to physical combat, and disciplines/gifts that raise your combat ability directly, and ignore all the &quot;autowin&quot; disciplines/gifts (I mean both splats have at higher levels enough powers of the type that if you optimise for them and go first in combat your opponent is done) I think the point where Vampires really get something that could pushes them in physical combat way above Werewolfs would be 6. Gen, and here specifically the Celerity Power &quot;Flower of Death&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think in actual game a Vampire Char surpassing a Werewolf Chat with the same amount of XP will likely ever happen, since Werewolfs just start more powerful and their Gifts are simply cheaper (not mention that you can cherry pick what gifts you want while vampires will often need to acquire some pretty lack lustre powers to get to the good stuff), and often more powerful than equivalent discipline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true.<br /> <br /> That's why I made starting build for Vampires and Werewolf, so we could compare starting values. And as starting chars, things are overwhelmingly in favour of Werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524207#post1524207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flower of Death is only for hand to hand, though, so you'd have to risk coming within arm's reach of a character with a staggeringly higher Strength (say, by using Gift of the Spriggan or Warp-Fury* for the most mid-tribe of all) and getting grappled. Spirit of the Fray means that they can wait for you to do this and interrupt you. Several tribes can also just flat out wait for you to waste massive amounts of blood trying to hit them while Strike the Air is engaged, and you'd need all the extra dice from Flower of Death just to try hitting a high-Rank Stargazer (literally nothing beats Circular Attack now, it can flat out give you Exalted-style perfect dodges in addition to being able to just redirect an attack to someone else).<br /> <br /> Of course, range is also a possible Achilles' heel for the lick you've proposed. Most of these solutions are Rank 3 or higher, but they're also in the style of &quot;dump damage on target, they have to deal with it&quot;, like Electroshock, which can be targeted from far off and rather unobtrusively just as long as the Glass Walker can connect a circuit. Red Talons, in contrast, can just howl at you if they can see you, and you take levels of lethal. Not agg, but they don't have to spend anything to do it.<br /> <br /> There's also Gift of the Giants, which allows Garou to Ultraman up to any size to become bigger than the biggest thing in the scene. A wonderfully versatile trick from Apocalypse that can be used in response to anything with higher physical stats than you to get higher stats than them. The only downside is that you're unlikely to learn it readily outside end of the world scenarios, where you typically have more important enemies to fight, like Grandmother Thunderwyrm or the zmei.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, there may be something from Vampire that outstrips Garou combat capacities, but it's not Flower of Death.<br /> <br /> *See Werewolf: the Wyld West. The tl;dr is that it's a potential one way ride that injures the Garou significantly at the end but boy does it pack a punch before that, basically doubling Crinos stats, and then some for Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I was looking at starting level gifts and fetishes. Or things that reasonably (even if difficult) you could have as a beginning Werewolf.<br /> <br /> If you get Spirit of the Fray starting (<i>Hummingbird </i>totem), then you simply win initiative. Initiative won, then it becomes a matter of establishing damage superiority, and that for werewolves tends to be brawl attacks, if the enemy are Vampires then there is a (relatively) cheap way to double damage (<i>Hunter's Talons</i> fetish).<br /> <br /> Then it is about having everyone else fight in your terms (brawl), that's where <i>Jam Weapon </i>comes into play.\u200b<br /> <br /> Esoteric attacks could be survived or overcome with specialist merits (<i>Untamable</i>) and maximum Willpower.<br /> <br /> You need to be able to avoid ambushes (<i>Sense Wyrm</i> helps), and some escape capabilities (<i>Mirrorshades </i>and high Gnosis)<br /> <br /> This is not perfect, still has gaps, but is as close to it as you can get with a starting character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-18-2023, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T23:13:27-07:00","id":1524260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524207#post1524207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several tribes can also just flat out wait for you to waste massive amounts of blood trying to hit them while Strike the Air is engaged, and you'd need all the extra dice from Flower of Death just to try hitting a high-Rank Stargazer (literally nothing beats Circular Attack now, it can flat out give you Exalted-style perfect dodges in addition to being able to just redirect an attack to someone else).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said I want to stick to mostly po powers that raise your combat powers directly. With all the other options it will get kind of messy, I mean vampires have also powers that will make them almost unhittable in combat (btw. the V20 Dark Age version of flower of Death also raises iirc also dodge and parry). And don't forget that a Vampire of Gen that could have Flower of Death could also have allready 14 dice for dodge or parry before using any other powers (I might overlook something since I'm not that famialr with Werewolf gifts, but iirc there is isn't much in terms of Gifts that raise and their attack and defence pools, most combat gifts either raise allow you to do more damage or soak more damage).<br /> <br /> When it comes to Grappling a 6th Gen Vampire could have a Strength of 7 (before using blood), Potence 7 (and with auto success those are basically worth two points of strength) and potentially some shapeshiftig Discipline like Protean or Vicissitude for some additional increase.<br /> <br /> I know getting all that together is pretty much impossible in play, but I still think if we are talking slugging it out in combat one on one, without using any tricks about gen 6 would be were vampires should have the numerical advantage (with an absurd amount of XP, which is likely much heigher than what you could reasonably spend on Werewolf).<br /> <br /> If we put no restriction on what powers can use for this comparison, I think we end up pretty fast with builds like a Koldun who could make Werewolfs spontaneously combust from several miles away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 10-19-2023, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T07:49:15-07:00","id":1524277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524260#post1524260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I said I want to stick to mostly po powers that raise your combat powers directly. With all the other options it will get kind of messy, I mean vampires have also powers that will make them almost unhittable in combat (btw. the V20 Dark Age version of flower of Death also raises iirc also dodge and parry).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean impossible to hit as in large numbers, I mean arbitrarily you can't hit them unless they leap into combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And don't forget that a Vampire of Gen that could have Flower of Death could also have allready 14 dice for dodge or parry before using any other powers (I might overlook something since I'm not that famialr with Werewolf gifts, but iirc there is isn't much in terms of Gifts that raise and their attack and defence pools, most combat gifts either raise allow you to do more damage or soak more damage). </div> </div> </div>Several soak Gifts can stack on top of each other, if you're going that route. If you got Troll Skin, Steel Fur, and Luna's Armor, you can rock some pretty hefty soak pools.<br /> <br /> But, as I noted, Circular Attack flat out provides perfect defenses in the style of Exalted, or similarly potent redirections. Also, you'd be surprised at how few damage adders that just add damage there are; usually, it's a boost to Strength. Garou using Might of Thor or Gift of the Spriggan, however, can get a ludicrous Strength pool for grappling, and as noted up thread, that can get decidedly nasty. Going another route, Fu Xi's Honor can add the character's permanent Honor rating to all their physical Attributes for a scene, given certain qualifiers like &quot;going after the Garou's family or friends&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to Grappling a 6th Gen Vampire could have a Strength of 7 (before using blood), Potence 7 (and with auto success those are basically worth two points of strength) and potentially some shapeshiftig Discipline like Protean or Vicissitude for some additional increase. </div> </div> </div>And the Garou could be 30 feet tall and 12 tonnes prior to using Gift of Giants to arbitrarily have higher physical attributes and greater size than you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know getting all that together is pretty much impossible in play, but I still think if we are talking slugging it out in combat one on one, without using any tricks about gen 6 would be were vampires should have the numerical advantage (with an absurd amount of XP, which is likely much heigher than what you could reasonably spend on Werewolf).<br /> <br /> If we put no restriction on what powers can use for this comparison, I think we end up pretty fast with builds like a Koldun who could make Werewolfs spontaneously combust from several miles away. </div> </div> </div>I put on my robe and wizard hat. I call the sun over the horizon with a level 6 rite. All vampires are incinerated everywhere. I'm declared the best there ever was!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T01:06:43-07:00","id":1524380,"title":"","content":"\u0130 have not been following the thread, but \u0130'm gonna put this here as it's relevant, \u0130 guess.<br /> <br /> We're playing VDA20, only core manual. \u0130 have a Warrior of Glycon, 7th gen, 116 xp or something similar.<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4, Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (but 4 when the event took place), Melee 3, Potence 5 (but 4 when the event below took place), Serpentis 4, Obfuscate 2.<br /> <br /> Before the summer a lone werewolf, Get of Fenris, Ahroun, rank 3, attacked the castle we were in for a vendetta against a coterie member. For various reasons my character ended up fighting him alone. \u0130 had the time to raise my attributes to 7 with blood and activate Serpentis 1 to 4, so physical attributes were at 9, and the tail had Strength 12. Note that the VDA20 manual has no rule that attributes can be raised to 10 max, and transformations were considered exceptions by the ST anyway, even with the max10 rule.<br /> <br /> Wolf has Spirit of the Frey, so he attacks first, trying to tackle me to throw me from the castle walls where we were fighting. Difficulty 8 because \u0130 am armed with sword and shield. He fails. \u0130 grab him with my tail (Serpentis 4), rolling 15 dice (the tail has Strength 12 instead of 9, plus Brawl which was 3 back then) and with Potence. \u0130t was difficulty 7 \u0130 think, because of declaring multiple actions, and 1 less dice, and \u0130 think \u0130 made some 7 success total. He's grabbed (hold). He had spent Rage to get 2 extra actions. He uses one to try and activate the Falling Touch gift thing, which fails (had it succeeded \u0130 would have argued that no physical law or game rule implies that falling forces one to release holds, so he might have fallen with me). With the second he tries to break my hold. He fails critically. The ST does not like to roll a thousand dice, so he declared that \u0130 succeeded without rolling at my next action that turn (biting him for blood with Typhonic Maw, drawing 5 blood points) given the critical failure. He had that gift to do aggravated damage with his blood, but \u0130 soaked it all thanks to Stamina 9 and Serpentis 3. As houserule, ST makes me roll for frenzy when drinking the blood. \u0130 fail, so \u0130 frenzy. Given the hold, the critical failure, the lack of other relevant gifts, and the statistical unlikeliness of him breaking the hold somehow, amd his being already half exsanguinated, the ST had the fight end there: next turn just had me finish drinking him and that's it.<br /> Later a coterie mate arrived, \u0130 attacked him in frenzy but he saved himself after some damage thanks to Rego Motus, and then Vladimir Rustovich arrived and complimented me for the swift kill.<br /> <br /> Rolls could have gone otherwise, \u0130 don't have his stats either - only know he had the Troll Skin gift for armour beyond those mentioned - and maybe he was statted with a bit less xp than me because he was the enemy of another coterie member with less xp, but this is how it went.<br /> <br /> We're currently going against more werewolves and one of our plans - maybe the favoured one - is to make them frenzy through a Malkavian and provocation and then \u0130 take them all if they don't attack each other, depending on their rage and gnosis scores.<br /> Without gifts due to frenzy, the worst they can have is be in crinos with Strength 9, Dext 6, Stam 8 and Brawl 5, and +4 to my difficulties due to multiple opponents. We did the maths and by raising my Stamina, doing a clinch with the tail to one of them every two turns (difficulty 10 but they don't dodge in frenzy and Potence gives me 5 automatic successes) - which deals enough damage to fill the track with bashing damage and making him lose consciousness for at least one turn - and killing him off with the tongue or bite to top up blood (he's unconscious, so no need to roll to hit at diff. 10) or with a squeeze of the clinch (no roll and enough damage to end him without Rage rolls to keep fighting) in the other turn, \u0130 can go forever killing one every 2 turns until the ST gets bored of rolling. The Stamina can be raised and kept raised to a level where they statistically can't make damage, and that's based on a fully optimised though frenzying Garou. They roll 10 dice to hit at diff 8 (wielding 2 great swords, so +2 diff to hit and -1 die too for reach) or 9 (if the Garou unconscious in my tail counts as some kind of shield) to hit and Strength 9 + the claw or bite damage (can't do anything else in berserker frenzy). \u0130 don't dodge, but soak with ever increasing Stamina (need to keep spending 1 blood point on it per turn to prevent it from dropping) at diff 5 (Serpentis 3) with specialisation. \u0130 can frenzy due to their blood, but it won't change my simple actions.<br /> The point is that low gen, experienced and optimised vampires can reach situations like this and hold off a raging werewolf army.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T02:40:22-07:00","id":1524381,"title":"","content":"Hold off a &quot;raging werewolf army&quot; that fights nothing like how the Garou are depicted as fighting, in an edition where all sorts of Garou powers and Gifts haven't been converted to account for the VDA20 base rules changes and thus aren't going to be as effective as they could be.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking VDA20, Potence requires spending blood for automatic successes. Spend 13 vitae on Attribute boosting and activating three Serpentis powers isn't leaving you a lot of turns to boost Potence as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T07:51:12-07:00","id":1524385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524381#post1524381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold off a &quot;raging werewolf army&quot; that fights nothing like how the Garou are depicted as fighting, in an edition where all sorts of Garou powers and Gifts haven't been converted to account for the VDA20 base rules changes and thus aren't going to be as effective as they could be.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking VDA20, Potence requires spending blood for automatic successes. Spend 13 vitae on Attribute boosting and activating three Serpentis powers isn't leaving you a lot of turns to boost Potence as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules of Werewolf 20 are actually quite good for the Werewolves themselves. Rage extra actions, for example, would probably have to change significantly. As it stands, I and every werewolf do 1 action with multiple actions penalties (+1 difficulty, -1 dice) unless they do not declare multiple actions; then every werewolf does all their rage actions, no penalty; then I and every werewolf do our multiple actions with increasing penalties (each one higher in difficulty by 1, and -1 more dice). Multiple actions (which are distinct from Rage, but not from VDA20 Celerity) cannot be used to do more than 1 attack unless you have things like extra limbs (Serpentis 2 gives you 1 extra tongue attack per turn, and Serpentis 4 one extra tail attack) or Velocity 3+ (your attack actions, instead of being the default 1, are half your Velocity dots rounded up), and penalties still apply (but Velocity mitigates them to some extent).<br /> <br /> True, things have not been converted, but we can't do much about that as a playing group. It's not like the ST has time to adapt the whole WtA20 rulebook to VDA20. However they do get the same mechanics as we do wherever applicable, and some things have not changed at all. So I think this is less of an issue than it's made out to seem. <br /> <br /> As for Potence, yes you spend 1 blood point per turn. I am a 7th gen and I am already pumped to 9 in all physical attributes and Serpentis powers are active. Currently I have 13 blood points in me, having recently fed. The scene is very complex, the coterie is divided in two different areas of the city and we're very slow at playing because we talk a lot, so the scene is being played over different sessions. I can spend 4 blood points per turn and drink 5 or 3 through bite or tongue. I cannot use multiple actions while fighting them all together because my difficulty goes to 10, which prevents multiple actions, otherwise I could use both bite and tongue and take 8 blood points. Each werewolf blood point is worth 2. This means that I spend 1 blood point (=bp) on Stamina each turn, and 1 on Potence every 2 turns and I regain up to 6 or 10 blood points every 2 turns, so the blood maths are fine. <br /> <br /> As for how Garou are depicted as fighting, the WtA20 manual clearly says that in berserker frenzy they only use claws, bites and running. It's a gibbous moon, their rage difficulty is 5. Our Malkavian is gonna use Incubus Humor on each while Obfuscated to make them even more irritable, lowering difficulty to 3. Then he's gonna taunt them because we entered their sacred house and killed some of their mates unnoticed to force them to roll Rage. Granted, some may have low Rage ratings and not frenzy because they just don't have enough dice to roll, but we're attacking a sept, not a pack, so even those in berserker frenzy with higher gnosis than rage will not attack their packmates, but will attack members of other packs. Before I've even left Obfuscate to join the fray and give them a target, they're gonna be at each other's throat. This may not be how Garou fight when they're in control, but here they are not. Vampires have schemed and planned and used mind tricks as they do, and gained a circumstantial advantage that might grant them a surprising victory. It is pretty consistent with the lore that werewolves are strong and scary, but are worse than vampires at controlling their temper and make fatal errors for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T08:18:42-07:00","id":1524386,"title":"","content":"What actually happens: the Fenrir sets up a bunch of Salamander's Scales around your domain, uses a Sun Crystal before engaging in close. You have nothing left to return to and will probably end up incinerated from the sunlight emanating from the Garou's necklace. See Werewolf: the Dark Ages pgs 116-117 and 121 for details. Note also that Fenrir Rank 3 means Might of Thor, which means getting a spear pitched into your heart from way off for 15-20 dice of damage plus attack successes as an opening gambit - none of this &quot;I rush up to the vampire for a grapple&quot; crap, even considering that it's also reasonable for such a character to have Catfeet (more Fenrir were lupus in those days than not), which grants -2 difficulty to tackling and grapples. Likely a few spears, actually, and the shield probably isn't going to last for more than one. Finally, it's also possible to have the pack patron be Firedrake, which means an effective Brawl of 7 is reasonable, and there's an extra reserve of four Rage points available.<br /> <br /> What actually happens in the mass combat plan: even more arson, even more Sun Crystals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T08:31:57-07:00","id":1524387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524385#post1524385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules of Werewolf 20 are actually quite good for the Werewolves themselves. Rage extra actions, for example, would probably have to change significantly. As it stands, I and every werewolf do 1 action with multiple actions penalties (+1 difficulty, -1 dice) unless they do not declare multiple actions; then every werewolf does all their rage actions, no penalty; then I and every werewolf do our multiple actions with increasing penalties (each one higher in difficulty by 1, and -1 more dice). Multiple actions (which are distinct from Rage, but not from VDA20 Celerity) cannot be used to do more than 1 attack unless you have things like extra limbs (Serpentis 2 gives you 1 extra tongue attack per turn, and Serpentis 4 one extra tail attack) or Velocity 3+ (your attack actions, instead of being the default 1, are half your Velocity dots rounded up), and penalties still apply (but Velocity mitigates them to some extent).<br /> <br /> True, things have not been converted, but we can't do much about that as a playing group. It's not like the ST has time to adapt the whole WtA20 rulebook to VDA20. However they do get the same mechanics as we do wherever applicable, and some things have not changed at all. So I think this is less of an issue than it's made out to seem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You apparently don't have much of a feel for the Garou, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Potence, yes you spend 1 blood point per turn. I am a 7th gen and I am already pumped to 9 in all physical attributes and Serpentis powers are active. Currently I have 13 blood points in me, having recently fed. The scene is very complex, the coterie is divided in two different areas of the city and we're very slow at playing because we talk a lot, so the scene is being played over different sessions. I can spend 4 blood points per turn and drink 5 or 3 through bite or tongue. I cannot use multiple actions while fighting them all together because my difficulty goes to 10, which prevents multiple actions, otherwise I could use both bite and tongue and take 8 blood points. Each werewolf blood point is worth 2. This means that I spend 1 blood point (=bp) on Stamina each turn, and 1 on Potence every 2 turns and I regain up to 6 or 10 blood points every 2 turns, so the blood maths are fine. </div> </div> </div>Taking in werewolf blood also means your difficulty to frenzy is likely to rise to 10. And once a vampire frenzies, they're overwhelmingly vulnerable from their lack of care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for how Garou are depicted as fighting, the WtA20 manual clearly says that in berserker frenzy they only use claws, bites and running. It's a gibbous moon, their rage difficulty is 5. Our Malkavian is gonna use Incubus Humor on each while Obfuscated to make them even more irritable, lowering difficulty to 3. Then he's gonna taunt them because we entered their sacred house and killed some of their mates unnoticed to force them to roll Rage. Granted, some may have low Rage ratings and not frenzy because they just don't have enough dice to roll, but we're attacking a sept, not a pack, so even those in berserker frenzy with higher gnosis than rage will not attack their packmates, but will attack members of other packs. Before I've even left Obfuscate to join the fray and give them a target, they're gonna be at each other's throat. This may not be how Garou fight when they're in control, but here they are not. Vampires have schemed and planned and used mind tricks as they do, and gained a circumstantial advantage that might grant them a surprising victory. It is pretty consistent with the lore that werewolves are strong and scary, but are worse than vampires at controlling their temper and make fatal errors for this. </div> </div> </div>This is a very vague plan written in crayon that assumes a lot of characters in close proximity to one another. And not, you know, rushing over to burn down the vampires' castles (arson is a very popular measure against vampires. High Rank Warders can even see through the flames and control them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T00:45:51-07:00","id":1524412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524277#post1524277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean impossible to hit as in large numbers, I mean arbitrarily you can't hit them unless they leap into combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have also several powers that can make them incorporeal and some can be activated instantaneously if someone attacks you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524277#post1524277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several soak Gifts can stack on top of each other, if you're going that route. If you got Troll Skin, Steel Fur, and Luna's Armor, you can rock some pretty hefty soak pools.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires have powers like Powers Rod Raw Rending and Eye for the Weakness of Steel that lets them ignore a certain amount of armor. there are also sevral powers that would allow a vampire to increase its strength even further, or to increase the damage of a weapon.<br /> Than there is the 5th level power of the Dur-An-Ki Path Awakening of the Steel lets you simply ignore all supernatural protection.<br /> And I think at least Troll Skin wouldn't work when the vampire uses a silver weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T05:17:41-07:00","id":1524420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524277#post1524277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, as I noted, Circular Attack flat out provides perfect defenses in the style of Exalted, or similarly potent redirections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looked it up. That a Role Wits+Athletics with a DC oppents Wits+3 (against a low Gen Vampire that could mean a difficulty of up to 10) to determine how many Attacks to can avoid, against a low gen Vampire can likely attack more often in turn than the Werewolf is going to have success.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T06:50:08-07:00","id":1524421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524412#post1524412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have also several powers that can make them incorporeal and some can be activated instantaneously if someone attacks you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorporeal can still be hit by Garou. Strike the Air, conversely, cannot be hit that way. Or any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires have powers like Powers Rod Raw Rending and Eye for the Weakness of Steel that lets them ignore a certain amount of armor. there are also sevral powers that would allow a vampire to increase its strength even further, or to increase the damage of a weapon.<br /> Than there is the 5th level power of the Dur-An-Ki Path Awakening of the Steel lets you simply ignore all supernatural protection.<br /> And I think at least Troll Skin wouldn't work when the vampire uses a silver weapon. </div> </div> </div>Bringing up silver just makes all the others seem superfluous. On the other hand, it'd also make you ping on Sense Silver, so the potential for ambushes is ruined. Finally, this still doesn't solve the &quot;set lots of fires&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looked it up. That a Role Wits+Athletics with a DC oppents Wits+3 (against a low Gen Vampire that could mean a difficulty of up to 10) to determine how many Attacks to can avoid, against a low gen Vampire can likely attack more often in turn than the Werewolf is going to have success. </div> </div> </div>Could be is no guarantee, especially given how expensive it is to raise Attributes. And the Stargazers are also conveniently the tribe with the Gift that lets them double up on spending Willpower, so there's a good likelihood you'll still be going up against one or two complete whiffs or &quot;oops I accidentally hit Karsh I hope he doesn't hold it against me!&quot; events, even at the high-botch difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T08:05:12-07:00","id":1524424,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5199\" data-vbnamecard=\"5199\">Aahz</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> You are both going higher and higher in experience, rank, power levels etc. At some point the comparison stopped being equivalent. That is why I insisted on doing this with starting characters.<br /> <br /> Paraphrasing from another forum: &quot;<i>Vampires start at 1 and theoretically can get to a 10 in power; Werewolves start at 4 and can get to a 6; the numbers are made up but give you an idea of the start and top for each</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, very low Generation vampires have no equal (what can compare with Plot Device power of Antediluvians?) but it is for all practical purposes impossible to get there as a character and would take insane amounts of experience.<br /> <br /> Yes, Werewolves start with obscene physical capabilities and narrow but potent gifts, but their higher levels powers are not that varied.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T09:01:35-07:00","id":1524427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524424#post1524424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5199\" data-vbnamecard=\"5199\">Aahz</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> You are both going higher and higher in experience, rank, power levels etc. At some point the comparison stopped being equivalent. That is why I insisted on doing this with starting characters.<br /> <br /> Paraphrasing from another forum: &quot;<i>Vampires start at 1 and theoretically can get to a 10 in power; Werewolves start at 4 and can get to a 6; the numbers are made up but give you an idea of the start and top for each</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, very low Generation vampires have no equal (what can compare with Plot Device power of Antediluvians?) but it is for all practical purposes impossible to get there as a character and would take insane amounts of experience.<br /> <br /> Yes, Werewolves start with obscene physical capabilities and narrow but potent gifts, but their higher levels powers are not that varied.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It did basically become a spillover for another thread, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T18:43:08-07:00","id":1524455,"title":"","content":"Something that is on a different axis from the &quot;1 to 10&quot; vs &quot;4 to 6&quot; issue though, is that the Garou have, for no direct XP costs, access to an nearly Mage-like level of versatility in three common Rites: Binding, Spirit Awakening, and Fetish. Garou having very cheap, and very early, access to magical items and no mechanical hurdles on what type of effects these items can do (aka mages needing Mind and Prime to make an amulet to protect them from mental Disciplines). While starting level Fetish crafters is pretty hard to pull off unless you take one of the Totems that boosts that, a starting level Talen crafting Theurge is barely a blip on starting character resources. The ability to pump out single use magical items of effects limited only by imagination and ST judgement is something to keep in consideration.<br /> <br /> While it might reduce the raw violence of the earlier starting level rawr-smash Garou if they have to make these things themselves, the ability to take the (small i on purpose) initiative from vampires in how much you can get out of preparation would vastly outdo a few less raw damage per hit in application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T22:37:37-07:00","id":1524468,"title":"","content":"I just reread the original post that started this thread. When does a combat-oriented vampire begin to match werewolves.<br /> I appreciate that comparison-wise it is easier to compare starting characters, but I think the question asked by the thread's originator would not be answered satisfactorily in this way. Choosing a certain amount of experience points and giving it to both a vampire and a garou seems better.<br /> <br /> That being said, without even needing to do those maths, something jumps to my attention: a combat-oriented vampire is one who invests most of his/her xp in Potence, Celerity, Fortitude, at least one combat ability (Brawl, Melee, Firearms) and physical attributes + generation (at start or via diablerie, since it can't be purchased with xp but changes greatly a character's martial prowess through ease of physical attributes boost). Such a vampire would usually manage to fulfill his blood and social needs with minimum further investment in complementary traits, since martial prowess can ensure patronage as a bodyguard of a socially powerful vampire or something similar or as tank for a coterie or underling for the sheriff. Some xp can go in Auspex, Obfuscate or Protean for additional rounding and versatility, though claws are not necessary at all: Potence ensures holds hold and Celerity ensures one can grapple with their opponent and bite him for aggravated damage in the same turn. Lethal weapons are also important to send enemies in torpor. A vampire will do all this and be a functional member of vampire society, and each and every of these dots will benefit him/her also in an encounter with Werewolves.<br /> By contrast, a combat oriented Garou, in terms of sheer physical attributes and related gifts, eventually falls behind such a vampire, and - and this is key - in order to remain functional in garou society, he/she has to buy other things with xp that have no or little use in a fight with a vampire because vampires are not the garou's only enemies. I think this makes a big difference, confirming what's already been said: young garou eat vampires, but old vampires eat garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, a garou specialised against vampires can buy many gifts and things to utterly incinerate them, but that's not nearly as common in garou society, just like vampires rarely specilalise in dealing with garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T22:43:22-07:00","id":1524469,"title":"","content":"We could say, a Garou is like Superman<br /> A Vampire? Is like Batman<br /> In a 1v1 white room scenario? A Garou would win 10 ouf of 10 (well depend of the storyteller really, for example Presence's Awe and Entrancement in some ST's eyes are a good and very dangerous way to have a puppy of your own... with (deadly) consequences on the long run)<br /> However just like Batman can beat anyone and anyting if he has enough time to prepare eg. he has time to analyze the threat and <i>prepare</i> for it accordingly, a Vampire similarly could beat a Garou in the right circumstances<br /> Ultimately it is up to your Storyteller<br /> I mean, if she wants you to have chance and beat the furball? Okay. Probably you will. If not? Not amount of miracles would save your behind and could quickly spiral down to powergaming - nothing wrong to have a superhero/villain with fangs, more often than not the games shift their focus from the personal horror to that angle, but keep in mind Vampire is a game that urses vampiric condition as a backdrop to explore themes of morality, depravity, the human condition (or appreciation of the human condition in its absence), salvation, and personal horror in a gloomy and exaggerated version of the real world<br /> But end of the day, the goal is to have fun<br /> It is possible to make a low (or high even) generation Garou-hunter/killer vampire?<br /> Yes<br /> Advised?<br /> No - unless you talked it through with your Storyteller and it fits to the Chronicle? Because if not? You will end up as a bolognese stain on the wall (or guacamole in case of a Nosferatu)\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-24-2023, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T23:00:43-07:00","id":1524470,"title":"","content":"And again, the almighty forum flag ate it on edit<br /> I don't even know why I bother to edit, knowing what will happen<br /> All right, let's do this one last time. My name is Peter Parker. I was bitten by a radioactive spider... <br /> Oppps, wrong<br /> But really, again:<br /> <br /> We could say, a Garou is like Superman<br /> A Vampire? Is like Batman<br /> In a 1v1 white room scenario? A Garou would win 10 ouf of 10 (well depend of the storyteller really, for example Presence's Awe and Entrancement in some ST's eyes are a good and very dangerous way to have a puppy of your own... with (deadly) consequences on the long run)<br /> However just like Batman can beat anyone and anyting if he has enough time to prepare eg. he has time to analyze the threat and <i>prepare</i> for it accordingly, a Vampire similarly could beat a Garou in the right circumstances<br /> Ultimately it is up to your Storyteller<br /> I mean, if she wants you to have chance and beat the furball? Okay. Probably you will. If not? Not amount of miracles would save your behind and could quickly spiral down to powergaming - nothing wrong to have a superhero/villain with fangs, more often than not the games shift their focus from the personal horror to that angle, but keep in mind Vampire is a game that urses vampiric condition as a backdrop to explore themes of morality, depravity, the human condition (or appreciation of the human condition in its absence), salvation, and personal horror in a gloomy and exaggerated version of the real world<br /> But end of the day, the goal is to have fun<br /> It is possible to make a low (or high even) generation Garou-hunter/killer vampire?<br /> Yes<br /> Advised?<br /> No - unless you talked it through with your Storyteller and it fits to the Chronicle? Because if not? You will end up as a bolognese stain on the wall (or guacamole in case of a Nosferatu)\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T00:01:22-07:00","id":1524471,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer not to get into the Bat God interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524468#post1524468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread the original post that started this thread. When does a combat-oriented vampire begin to match werewolves.<br /> I appreciate that comparison-wise it is easier to compare starting characters, but I think the question asked by the thread's originator would not be answered satisfactorily in this way. Choosing a certain amount of experience points and giving it to both a vampire and a garou seems better.<br /> <br /> That being said, without even needing to do those maths, something jumps to my attention: a combat-oriented vampire is one who invests most of his/her xp in Potence, Celerity, Fortitude, at least one combat ability (Brawl, Melee, Firearms) and physical attributes + generation (at start or via diablerie, since it can't be purchased with xp but changes greatly a character's martial prowess through ease of physical attributes boost). Such a vampire would usually manage to fulfill his blood and social needs with minimum further investment in complementary traits, since martial prowess can ensure patronage as a bodyguard of a socially powerful vampire or something similar or as tank for a coterie or underling for the sheriff. Some xp can go in Auspex, Obfuscate or Protean for additional rounding and versatility, though claws are not necessary at all: Potence ensures holds hold and Celerity ensures one can grapple with their opponent and bite him for aggravated damage in the same turn. Lethal weapons are also important to send enemies in torpor. A vampire will do all this and be a functional member of vampire society, and each and every of these dots will benefit him/her also in an encounter with Werewolves.<br /> By contrast, a combat oriented Garou, in terms of sheer physical attributes and related gifts, eventually falls behind such a vampire, and - and this is key - in order to remain functional in garou society, he/she has to buy other things with xp that have no or little use in a fight with a vampire because vampires are not the garou's only enemies. I think this makes a big difference, confirming what's already been said: young garou eat vampires, but old vampires eat garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, a garou specialised against vampires can buy many gifts and things to utterly incinerate them, but that's not nearly as common in garou society, just like vampires rarely specilalise in dealing with garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-point: Rage is way cheaper than Celerity, and Gifts are way cheaper and individually selectable, and in many cases varied than Disciplines. Also, having a spiritual patron and backing from Ancestors can help push Garou over the point where vampires would be even remotely comfortable dealing with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T00:31:27-07:00","id":1524472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524471#post1524471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer not to get into the Bat God interpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Counter-point: Rage is way cheaper than Celerity, and Gifts are way cheaper and individually selectable, and in many cases varied than Disciplines. Also, having a spiritual patron and backing from Ancestors can help push Garou over the point where vampires would be even remotely comfortable dealing with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell you what: post a 150 xp garou character sheet using only the W20 manual. You can build it for what you want, including combat, but NOT a specialised vampire hunter. \u0130 will do the same, with a combat oriented vampire, 150 xp, VtM20 only, not based on your own sheet, NOT a specialised werewolf hunter.<br /> <br /> They meet casually one night doing their business and start a fight. They both call their buddies in as they prefer, but it will take at least 1 minute (10 turns) for the buddies to come, so we won't factor them in to avoid having to stat out the rest of the pack, the ghouls, the coterie, etc.<br /> <br /> Let's see where it goes. Let's be specific and concrete instead of just listing the hundred possible powers and advantages each could have.<br /> <br /> ED\u0130T: to be clear, \u0130 mean we're both going to use only the core manual of each splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 10-24-2023, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T03:48:04-07:00","id":1524473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524471#post1524471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter-point: Rage is way cheaper than Celerity, and Gifts are way cheaper and individually selectable, and in many cases varied than Disciplines. Also, having a spiritual patron and backing from Ancestors can help push Garou over the point where vampires would be even remotely comfortable dealing with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to forget that the Werewolf allready starts with the equivalent of 10 discipline points. And that some Gifts are just more powerfull than a single point in a physical discipline.<br /> I mean Lunars Armor is easily as strong as something like 3-5 points in fortitude.<br /> <br /> The biggest advantage Vampire have imo is that they can (with low generation) get their powers faster online, with some of them also being permanently on and many only needing free actions for activation and that they don't have the problem that some of their powers prevent them from getting extra Actions with Celerity on the same turn, while Werwolfs afaik can't spend Gnosis and range on the same turn.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T13:17:29-07:00","id":1524485,"title":"","content":"Rage and Gnosis - Unless a Gift requires it, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524472#post1524472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell you what: post a 150 xp garou character sheet using only the W20 manual. You can build it for what you want, including combat, but NOT a specialised vampire hunter. \u0130 will do the same, with a combat oriented vampire, 150 xp, VtM20 only, not based on your own sheet, NOT a specialised werewolf hunter.<br /> <br /> They meet casually one night doing their business and start a fight. They both call their buddies in as they prefer, but it will take at least 1 minute (10 turns) for the buddies to come, so we won't factor them in to avoid having to stat out the rest of the pack, the ghouls, the coterie, etc.<br /> <br /> Let's see where it goes. Let's be specific and concrete instead of just listing the hundred possible powers and advantages each could have.<br /> <br /> ED\u0130T: to be clear, \u0130 mean we're both going to use only the core manual of each splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Renown? And are you still going with Strength + Intimidation as not just a viable dice pool, but also something more effective than Dominate? Because that's going to be a major deal-breaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T15:04:50-07:00","id":1524487,"title":"","content":"Also, what about Rites? Rites don't cost XP to learn. You can, if you have a decent roll, you can easily learn dozens of them in a year. As I noted above, some of them open up a world of non-XP powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T18:37:13-07:00","id":1524493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524485#post1524485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage and Gnosis - Unless a Gift requires it, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What about Renown? And are you still going with Strength + Intimidation as not just a viable dice pool, but also something more effective than Dominate? Because that's going to be a major deal-breaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 gave you the quote in the other thread from the Werewolf manual showing that Strength + \u0130ntimidation is totally a thing for werewolves like for anyone else. You insisted with your bizarre theory that Garou are unphased by Strength, but have not quoted any manual supporting your idea.<br /> And it's not stronger than Dominate: Dominate is a single direct order and a single roll; intimidation is a contrasted roll and has a different effect and psychological impact. As a contrasted roll, it is already less effective than Dominate generally, because less successes will pass. Dominate, however, is a supernatural trick and there are ways around it. \u0130ntimidation is a natural thing, and there are other ways around it (like frenzying), but it may help in some situations more than Dominate - or less. Same as Presence.<br /> <br /> As for rites, as well as backgrounds, \u0130 kept mine to a minimum. \u0130 think it makes more sense to ignore rites and backgrounds for a 1 minute chance fight neither party was planning for.<br /> <br /> As for Renown or rank, \u0130 need to look again at the manual, but it's late where \u0130 am: will need to get back to it in a few hours","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T19:11:45-07:00","id":1524495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524493#post1524493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u0130 gave you the quote in the other thread from the Werewolf manual showing that Strength + \u0130ntimidation is totally a thing for werewolves like for anyone else. You insisted with your bizarre theory that Garou are unphased by Strength, but have not quoted any manual supporting your idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>My pdf of W20 does not list Strength + Intimidation as one of the recommended combinations of At + Ab, and that there's only an ST-determined bonus to Manipulation + Intimidation based on what you do with your Strength, because that's exactly what W20 says to do. In Facedowns, in Interrogations, and in Intimidation, Strength is considered less scary than Rage by way of omitting Strength from having much, if anything, to do with those rolls. The proof is in the total lack of system interaction or engagement for using Strength as a way to threaten. The relevant sections start on page 227. Good luck finding anything specifically talking about Strength.<br /> <br /> As to being unfazed, not so. They would immediately attack you even if not inclined. As I pointed out multiple times, if your intent as a non-Garou is to show to Garou that you are a strong threat, you've just shown yourself to be worth at least half a permanent dot of Glory. Don't blame me if the message that you were broadcasting has a... different meaning to a warrior culture specifically dedicated to killing the kind of beings that your character happens to fall under.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's not stronger than Dominate: Dominate is a single direct order and a single roll; intimidation is a contrasted roll and has a different effect and psychological impact. As a contrasted roll, it is already less effective than Dominate generally, because less successes will pass. Dominate, however, is a supernatural trick and there are ways around it. \u0130ntimidation is a natural thing, and there are other ways around it (like frenzying), but it may help in some situations more than Dominate - or less. Same as Presence. </div> </div> </div>Come on, you were trying to get Garou to turn away from Gaia and declare their faith in Sutekh! You were totally treating your roll as better than Dominate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for rites, as well as backgrounds, \u0130 kept mine to a minimum. \u0130 think it makes more sense to ignore rites and backgrounds for a 1 minute chance fight neither party was planning for. </div> </div> </div>Not really how rites work, since they're a part of a Garou's life. The rite of binding and rite of summoning, together, are a momentous change to outlook and daily approaches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Renown or rank, \u0130 need to look again at the manual, but it's late where \u0130 am: will need to get back to it in a few hours </div> </div> </div>No issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T19:14:18-07:00","id":1524496,"title":"","content":"Except the Garou are part of a militant society. Carrying magical items they gain from rites is as usual for them as a soldier carrying a gun or a blade. This is especially the case as many Talens appear innocuous to even other supernatural creatures that don't know about Garou culture, and such items are not restricted like normal items when shapeshifting or side-stepping into the Umbra. A Garou would need to perform a rite to bring a non-rite enhanced weapon with them everywhere, so they're naturally going to opt for rite-made weapons/tools to give them more options for dedicating other items.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just skip rites,&quot; means we're not really comparing Garou to vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T23:46:52-07:00","id":1524499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> regarding rites, renown, rank, carried fetish and talens, obviously there is no &quot;rule&quot; as they're not bought with experience. Our test guy might be a very accomplished guy or might not be. What we have fixed is that s/he has 150 xp. I leave it to the WtA experts to judge whether the amounts chosen by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> for these traits are reasonable. <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Strength + Intimidate is listed at p.266 of VtM20 corebook and given as an example roll at p.240 of WtA20 corebook, as I said in the other thread. Also, vampire warrior cultures of clans and bloodlines with Potence would be even more entitled to not get bothered by Strength, but no such rule exists. Simply, warrior cultures cultivate Strength and Intimidation, thus naturally get better at that roll, and supernatural warrior cultures add their own supernatural bonuses to it, getting even less likely to be intimidated. But they still get intimidated by people with even higher supernatural might, unless they have a power to avoid that. <br /> As for me making the roll better than Dominate to convert people to Sutekh: I did a pretty normal thing for a religious fanatic to do in the Middle Ages, and a rather common interaction between warring people: I shouted convert or die and displayed strength. That takes a normal roll. My character happened to have a staggering -6 difficulty to that roll thanks to 2 disciplline powers (Serpentis 1 + Serpentis 3), a supernatural merit (Powerful Aura) and an extremely rare Road rating of 10, along with very high supernatural Strength. This led the roll to average - assuming a +4 to difficulty due to being outnumbered - to 7 successes more than the average number rolled by a crinos with Strength 9, Intimidate 5 and a relevant specialisation (7 successes on difficulty 6), which would not even be the case for most garou in the scene. 5 excess successes on a roll give &quot;phenomenal&quot; results by the VtM20 manual and &quot;Phenomenal; you perform with perfection, or you\u2019ve created lasting greatness&quot; by the VDA20 manual. We're talking 7\u0300+ successes here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T07:47:54-07:00","id":1524502,"title":"","content":"What I see on page 240 is part of a shotgunning of haphazard examples left over from days of the distant past - like, literally this is almost verbatim from 1e but tweaked to be about another werewolf (page 87 in case you were curious). Since 1e, W:tA has formalized a very different set of rules involving Intimidation, and while technically there's nothing that says that you have to use any given rule, the authors wrote them into W20, so I'm damn well going to be using them. Blatant displays of force are a bonus likely lesser in effect than using Manipulation + Intimidation or Rage (2e suggested only two dice for tearing a fomor apart, so smashing some stonework is probably not going to rate very highly). Loose bits of early system sketching do not a robust rules system make, and I see no reason to turn back the clock on it. Shit's old, and the ship has sailed; lots of people since have done systems work, and I don't think that just tearing them up for an incredibly self-indulgent attempt to browbeat Garou with Potence is a good reason to continue to coddle those rules.<br /> <br /> Further, what you do not seem to grasp about the warrior culture of the Garou is that, given the existence of Rage, they have elaborate ritual systems put in place to avoid more outbreaks of berserk killing than are already a risk just from having Rage. Mediating these disputes is the life's calling of an entire auspice (the Philodox), and places them in between wild murder machines on a regular basis. Strength is secondary to this task; they need Willpower and social graces to get through some damnably impenetrable hides and skulls so that they can actually put a stop to this shit without escalating it. To that end, Garou society really does not seem to put much value in your ability to do the violence. This ability is already incredibly high in every werewolf; if you want it to mean something to others, you either need to be very good at talking or else have had the spirits and Garou society vouch for you in the form of Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T07:51:27-07:00","id":1524523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524472#post1524472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ED\u0130T: to be clear, \u0130 mean we're both going to use only the core manual of each splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And which crossover rules will you use, praytell?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:34:19-07:00","id":1524542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524523#post1524523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And which crossover rules will you use, praytell?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Give me specific issues and \u0130'll tell you what \u0130 think appropriate about that. Otherwise we would figure it out with the other person who participates in this. Otherwise \u0130 genuinely don't get what this thread is about.<br /> <br /> \u0130f we simply assume the two splats are not to be mixed rules-wise, the answer to the original question is relative to the ST's decisions on how to handle werewolves as enemies in a vampire game (since \u0130 figure this was the context of the original question).<br /> \u0130f we assume they can, in some way, be made to interact, then naturally there is no straight answer to the thread's question, but it will depend on the build of the characters involved, the circumstances of their encounter, and how good the players or the ST are at using their advantages and disadvantages.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe reason for my suggestion, however, was because it had been repeatedly stated that a young Garou trashes a new vampire, but an old vampire can trash an old Garou assuming that neither is specialised in hunting the other or has prepared for some surprise attack leveraging all sorts of social, mental, physical and supernatural shenanigans. \u0130 generally agree with this idea, if the vampire is combat oriented (but not specialised against lupines). Otherwise he will use prep and social shenanigans as expected.<br /> <br /> To avoid dragging the discussion by simply listing all kind of hypothetical advantage each splat has over the other (which would demand an answer to your same question: by which crossover rules? - and indeed your question has to be answered regardless by anyone dealing with this thread, in some way), \u0130 proposed a simple test of builds in a random physical encounter. Nobody has posted a character sheet yet, mine's ready, but \u0130've quite lost interest in the discussion at this point to be honest.<br /> <br /> Anyway, considering that this is the VtM forum and the original question of the thread seems to have been from the point of view of a vampire player, \u0130 would give priority to VtM over WtA when there is a conflict in crossover rules, but it has to be checked case by case, because in some situations that might be inappropriate. Likewise, if this was a post in the WtA forum, \u0130'd give priority to WtA over VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T13:22:10-07:00","id":1524547,"title":"","content":"I'm asking because there are multiple sets of crossover rules for how powers interact with each other, I'm just curious how you decide which ones are right. It's one of the elements that makes the whole exercise rather more complicated than you think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T15:47:20-07:00","id":1524553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524547#post1524547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking because there are multiple sets of crossover rules for how powers interact with each other, I'm just curious how you decide which ones are right. It's one of the elements that makes the whole exercise rather more complicated than you think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 don't see why you assume \u0130 see it as less complicated than how you see it. My first posts in this thread acknowledged immediately the complexity of the variables. But either such complexity leads one to drop the discussion altogether, or one goes ahead nonetheless with producing concrete characters and situations and making an approximated but informed and reasoned out judgment. The third option is going in circles about the whole thing neither admitting it's an issue with no clear cut answer nor providing a convincing and well reasoned assessment like &quot;provided these limited test conditions, generally speaking this splat will have the statistic advantage&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T16:24:00-07:00","id":1524554,"title":"","content":"But you can't really expect people to build example characters without addressing at least some crossover issues. For example, do we use the V20 weapon char, or the W20 weapon chart? That's going to seriously impact what kind of Garou someone might make for the exercise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T18:47:52-07:00","id":1524561,"title":"","content":"I'm still stuck on the &quot;just go with anything&quot; for Renown and Rank. Handwaving away Renown and Rank is a lot like handwaving away Conviction and Virtues for Imbued, or Tao for the way that hsien used to work, and possibly some Mummy details that I can't remember very well. You can't really make an xp equivalence for it, either, because it doesn't interact with it. And, unlike Deeds in Weapons of the Gods, you can continue to accumulate Renown even when your Rank doesn't go up; you could potentially get a permanent Glory of 10 while still a cliath.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's a character that doesn't use Renown and sets Rank at whatever your superiors and their literally divine supervisors think you should be at, but you probably aren't looking to compare vampires to Nagah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T00:13:11-07:00","id":1524574,"title":"","content":"Alright friends, let's drop the character test thing then. Crossover issues relevant to a 1-minute street fight could be figured out one by one, but then it would create a very specific set of decisions and it would produce a very questionable result, so not worth even getting into it.<br /> \u0130 leave the discussion concluding for myself that WtA and VtM are not objectively comparable and the answer to the original thread's question depends on a lot of variables, including how the ST chooses to handle werewolves in a VtM game (or viceversa).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T08:19:48-07:00","id":1524588,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> if you're interested in the topic with a set of fixed ground rules for White Room combat, there was a brilliant series of fights as mapped out on characters with proper ground rules and some code running a thousand iterations of each conflict to actually see how these things work out in a White Room context, that you've been postulating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup/page3\">The preliminary discussion starts here</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup\">The events </a><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis\">wrap up here with an analysis</a> (+ a link to all the individual threads with the different competitors1)<br /> <br /> Kudos to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4851\" data-vbnamecard=\"4851\">Cheesefondue</a> for applying the time honored art of statistics to what has traditionally been a playground spat. <br /> <br /> Once you start going into exotic interactions and how different the systems are it's much harder to map things out, and it's always possible to find a tool to do horrible things to the opposition. But since those are dependant on the table, the storyteller, the game being played and the context, it's hard to find an &quot;objective&quot; truth. Cheesefondue's work is probably the closest we've ever gotten to a sensible set of guidelines and how mechanics interact in the WoD when at a even playing field (which doesn't really happen in a normal game anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T12:14:43-07:00","id":1524655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1524588#post1524588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> if you're interested in the topic with a set of fixed ground rules for White Room combat, there was a brilliant series of fights as mapped out on characters with proper ground rules and some code running a thousand iterations of each conflict to actually see how these things work out in a White Room context, that you've been postulating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup/page3\">The preliminary discussion starts here</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769128-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup\">The events </a><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis\">wrap up here with an analysis</a> (+ a link to all the individual threads with the different competitors1)<br /> <br /> Kudos to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4851\" data-vbnamecard=\"4851\">Cheesefondue</a> for applying the time honored art of statistics to what has traditionally been a playground spat.<br /> <br /> Once you start going into exotic interactions and how different the systems are it's much harder to map things out, and it's always possible to find a tool to do horrible things to the opposition. But since those are dependant on the table, the storyteller, the game being played and the context, it's hard to find an &quot;objective&quot; truth. Cheesefondue's work is probably the closest we've ever gotten to a sensible set of guidelines and how mechanics interact in the WoD when at a even playing field (which doesn't really happen in a normal game anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T10:55:20-07:00","id":1537865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1523828#post1523828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This was a strong build, but I think I have an even stronger one now, again 7 points of flaws needed, must use the optional ruling to start with 4 dots in Disciplines but no Background dots (V20 Core p.85) and makes use of the rules for Necromancy to use Willpower rolls (V20 Rites of the Blood p.130):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Clan: Harbingers of Skulls<br /> Nature: Sociopath<br /> Demeanor: Idealist<br /> Generation: 13th<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 5 (Dodging), Stamina 2<br /> Social: Charisma 1, Manipulation 4 (Guile), Appearance 0<br /> Mental: Perception 4 (Sharp Senses), Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Combat Reflexes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics 3, Investigation 3, Occult 3<br /> Disciplines: Necromancy 5 (Path of the Four Humors 5)<br /> Necromantic Rituals: Death\u2019s Communion<br /> Backgrounds: Memento de Morte 5, Spirit Slaves 1<br /> Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Derangements: Megalomania<br /> Merits: Mortuario<br /> Flaws: Kiss of Death, Inbred 5 (Derangement)<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 10/1<br /> <br /> <br /> The build can kill everything around them at an unbeatable DC, it is at risk of going late in the initiative order, but if not killed by the initial attack, it autowins, key elements of the build:<ul><li>Clan: Harbingers of Skulls (<i>to be able to start with Path of the Four Humors</i>).</li> <li>Necromancy 5 / Path of the Four Humors 5 (<i>Black Breath is DEADLY: unsoakable area of effect attack</i>).</li> <li>Willpower: 10 (<i>the key stat rolled for Necromancy Paths</i>).</li> <li>Derangements: Megalomania (<i>an extra die on Willpower rolls</i>).</li> <li>Background: Memento de Morte 5 (<i>+5 dice to Necromancy rolls</i>).</li> <li>Background: Spirit Slaves 1 (<i>invisible intangible spy who obeys your every command, can create fires and move objects, guard your house during the day, talk to ghosts and do lots of sensitive tasks for you</i>).\u200b</li> <li>Necromantic Rituals: Death\u2019s Communion (<i>+2</i><i> dice to Necromancy rolls, maybe as a Harbinger of Skulls this Ritual is not available</i>).\u200b\u200b</li> <li>Perception 4, Alertness and Awareness 3 (<i>to detect ambushes and react fast</i>).</li> <li>Dexterity 5 and Wits 5 (<i>for initiative</i><i>; Dodge specialty for Dexterity; Ambushes specialty for Wits</i>).</li> <li>Athletics 3 (<i>with Dexterity 5 and this, a high chance of avoiding attacks)</i>.</li> <li>Stealth 3 (<i>with Dexterity 5 and this, a high chance of staying hidden)</i>.\u200b</li> <li>Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5</li> <li>Merit: Mortuario (<i>-2 diff to Necromancy rolls!!!</i>).</li> <li>Flaws: Kiss of Death, Inbred 5 (Derangement) (<i>to have enough points for the build and get Megalomania</i>).</li> </ul><br /> This is probably the DEADLIEST starting vampire build. At least 16 dice at DC 6 (18 dice if you have the ritual up beforehand, so between 6 and 7 successes), area of effect of 5 meters in diameter per success, if you do not dodge (Dexterity + Athletics) it requires to roll Willpower (DC 8 for mortals or DC 7 for supers) and get more successes than the attacker, or immediately commit suicide if living/fall into torpor if Kindred, it is nearly impossible to get 7 or 8 successes rolling 10 Willpower dice, so those who do not dodge are dead.<br /> <br /> Using Harbingers of Skulls due to starting Necromancy paths, but I think this could be done with a Giovanni... And that releases 2 freebies more to be put into the Spirit Slaves Background, get some Wraiths that help you if you don't win initiative or in the unlikely scenario of enemies surviving the attack.<br /> <br /> You could also use the Nagaraja, and the Vitreous Path. It becomes a single attack, but using Night Cry on yourself as a buff, and then attacking will do around 11 aggravated damage in a single attack against a target. More survivable than the first option if hit, but also more likely to hit.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread has gone through a lot, but I think I have another build for this, again 7 points of flaws needed, must use the optional ruling to start with 4 dots in Disciplines but no Background dots (V20 Core p.85):<br /> <br /> <br /> Clan: Ravnos (Brahman)<br /> Nature: Conniver<br /> Demeanor: Trickster<br /> Generation: 8th<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 4 (Dodging), Stamina 1<br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 5 (Misdirection), Appearance 1<br /> Mental: Perception 4 (Sharp Senses), Intelligence 1, Wits 5 (Ambushes)<br /> Talents: Alertness 3, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Intimidation 1, Subterfuge 5 (Illusions)<br /> Skills: Animal Ken 3, Drive 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 1, Survival 3<br /> Knowledges: Computer 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Law 1, Technology 1<br /> Disciplines: Chimerstry 4<br /> Backgrounds: Generation 5<br /> Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Merits: Concentration, Eidetic Memory, Vitae Mutation<br /> Flaws: Catspaw, Infertile Vitae<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 15/3\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> The build can access Chimerstry 5 at low cost, it is at risk of going late in the initiative order, but if not killed by the initial attack, it uses Horrid Reality to do terrible things, key elements of the build:<ul><li>Clan: Ravnos Brahman (<i>to have Auspex</i> <i>eventually</i>).\u200b</li> <li>Chimerstry 4 (<i>why not 5? Keep reading</i>).\u200b</li> <li>Willpower: 10 (<i>the main fuel for</i> <i>Chimerstry</i>).\u200b</li> <li>Background: Generation 5 (<i>better blood pool, immune to Dominate from higher generations</i>\u200b).\u200b</li> <li>Perception 4, Alertness and Awareness 3 (<i>to detect ambushes and react fast</i>).</li> <li>Dexterity 4 and Wits 5 (<i>for initiative</i><i>; Dodge specialty for Dexterity; Ambushes specialty for Wits</i>).</li> <li>Athletics 3 (<i>With Dexterity 4 and this, a high chance of avoiding attacks)</i>.</li> <li>Subterfuge 5 (<i>with an illusions specialty when we get to the merits this will make sense</i>)</li> <li>Virtues: Conscience 1, Self-Control 4, Courage 5</li> <li>Merit: Concentration. (<i>to ignore circumstantial penalties to dice pools or difficulty ratings, helpful to manifest illusions in a stressful situation</i>).</li> <li>\u200bMerit: Eidetic Memory (<i>the illusions are perfect, I say PERFECT</i>).</li> <li>\u200bMerit: Vitae Mutation (<i>this is the power and the glory, once per night you roll Willpower at diff 7, and on A SINGLE success you get access to 1 extra dot of Chimerstry! Since we already have Willpower 10, we can not fail the roll and get access to the fifth Chimerstry</i>\u200b<i> dot, cheaper than buying it directly with freebies</i>).\u200b</li> <li>Flaws: Catspaw, Infertile Vitae. (<i>to have enough points for the build</i>).</li> </ul>If you allow 'Vitae Mutation' to grant dots above 5, you can get rid of Generation 5 and the last dot of Subterfuge to buy Chimerstry 5. Now with the sixth dot of Chimerstry get &quot;Fatuus Mastery&quot;, eliminating the Willpower and Blood cost of the first 3 levels of Chimerstry!!! Broken? Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-08-2026, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T20:31:24-07:00","id":1538018,"title":"","content":"Remember that, <br /> <br /> Vampires, hunt mortals.<br /> Werewolves, hunt other supernatural, &quot;Things&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T23:25:32-07:00","id":1538027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1538018#post1538018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that,<br /> <br /> Vampires, hunt mortals.<br /> Werewolves, hunt other supernatural, &quot;Things&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less about hunting, more about turning them into ludicrous gibs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T23:15:25-07:00","id":1541960,"title":"","content":"A lot of the metafiction for these encounters have a lot of &quot;Plot Armor.&quot; Mithras should have been torn to pieces if he just came out of torpor, even with the excuse &quot;He was weak from torpor,&quot; but still slaughtered a pack of Lupines.<br /> <br /> It's the same excuse of why an Archmage just can't teleport a Methuselah or Antediluvian into the photosphere of the sun. <br /> <br /> &quot;Plot Armor.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But... but... paradox...&quot;<br /> <br /> Whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T23:18:34-07:00","id":1541961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302757#post1302757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires always have access to such power, it's that developing it all over time that matters. While there are certainly Elder level Disciplines that make you even tougher in combat, and the extra blood pool and blood per turn is nice, and the ability to buy higher base traits... you don't need any of that. Potence 5 and a silver weapon is enough to do in most 'entry' level werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not a &quot;Sure Thing.&quot; <br /> <br /> Gen 6 is when you can mop the floor with 1 or 2 lupines, But like stated earlier, that is for that gen being around long enough to have decent physical stats and disciplines.<br /> <br /> A 6th gen neonate is going down fast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T23:30:37-07:00","id":1541962,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what you're trying to say by responding to me and citing my other posts in the thread as to why I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T01:46:03-07:00","id":1541966,"title":"","content":"He's not interested in debating Heavy Arms and just ignore him or report him. All he does is show up once in awhile and spam nearly dead threads or make broad statements like the ones you mentioned and not explain his reasoning in any great detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-12-2024, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T18:47:42-07:00","id":1542011,"title":"","content":"In regards to Mages, don't they need to know things in order to make best use of there magic? If I wanted to get the best results of life magic, I think it would be quite useful to have a solid understanding of the human body if Mage The Awakening is any indictation. So in that case wouldn't I have to understand the vast distance of where the sun is from Earth to do a powerful teleportation spell? And not to mention it sounds like that I would be bending the rules of reality to a huge degree and get serious blowback.<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Mage is limited to the Awakening the line and not the Ascension line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2024, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T20:24:04-07:00","id":1542014,"title":"","content":"Ascension doesn't lean on mundane knowledge to get the best spells like Awakening does via Rote Skills.<br /> <br /> How much mundane knowledge matters in Ascension is very tied to how the individual mage operates. An Ascension mage that heals through faith and prayer would benefit more from knowing the proper prayers in their religion for healing than they would studying the Medicine Knowledge. One that uses technomagic most certainly does need to have a good understanding of Medicine and/or Science for healing magic.<br /> <br /> In Awakening terms, mundane skills in Ascension can be used as a basic Yantra but isn't particularly great (esp. since in Ascension you roll it and how much of a benefit you get is based on the roll where most spell casting bonuses don't). There's an optional rule in M20 where you can use a whole Ability as one of the simpler unrolled flat bonuses, but then you need to keep your rating high.<br /> <br /> Ascension also really don't have Paradox (said blow back) care too much about how huge of a degree you're bending reality: it's based on the highest Sphere used in the spell (which does play into that). How much you're bending reality goes into how many successes you need to pull something off instead. So if you're using a Correspondence 4 spell that requires a few successes to create a temporary gateway between two mage's homes so the group can move back and forth, or if you're trying to open a portal to the sun? You're facing a much harder roll to succeed at, but the same amount of blow back if you mess it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T10:41:11-07:00","id":1542066,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer about different Mage The Awakening works from Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}